osition and load order.** `packages/unipi/index.ts` is the single composition root. The verified sequence is:"},"215":{"id":"/docs/architecture-213","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#32-domain-module-architecture","content":"Two properties of this ordering are architecturally significant. First, `createUnipiTracer(pi)` produces `tracer.scope(name)`, a proxy around the `ExtensionAPI` that fingerprints hook inputs/outputs so trajectory can attribute context mutations to individual packages. Second, the order is **load-bearing**: `utility` must precede `info-screen` because the TUI overlay stack pops top-most entries and a capturing overlay's `done()` is one-shot. This contract is currently enforced only by a comment in the composition root."},"216":{"id":"/docs/architecture-214","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#33-storage-design","content":"Persistence is file- and SQLite-based; there is no network database. Each store is owned by exactly one package."},"217":{"id":"/docs/architecture-215","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#33-storage-design","content":"Store"},"218":{"id":"/docs/architecture-216","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#33-storage-design","content":"Location"},"219":{"id":"/docs/architecture-217","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#33-storage-design","content":"Format"},"220":{"id":"/docs/architecture-218","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#33-storage-design","content":"Owner"},"221":{"id":"/docs/architecture-219","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#33-storage-design","content":"Consistency mechanism"},"222":{"id":"/docs/architecture-220","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#33-storage-design","c