_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#511-exception-handling-mechanisms","content":"`web-api/engine/extract.ts`"},"521":{"id":"/docs/architecture-519","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#511-exception-handling-mechanisms","content":"Invalid `ask_user` format"},"522":{"id":"/docs/architecture-520","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#511-exception-handling-mechanisms","content":"Validation error returned to agent"},"523":{"id":"/docs/architecture-521","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#511-exception-handling-mechanisms","content":"`ask-user/tools.ts`"},"524":{"id":"/docs/architecture-522","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#511-exception-handling-mechanisms","content":"Dangerous sandbox command"},"525":{"id":"/docs/architecture-523","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#511-exception-handling-mechanisms","content":"Security scanner/evaluator blocks; env vars scrubbed"},"526":{"id":"/docs/architecture-524","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#511-exception-handling-mechanisms","content":"`compactor/security/*`, `executor.ts`"},"527":{"id":"/docs/architecture-525","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#511-exception-handling-mechanisms","content":"Overflowing result"},"528":{"id":"/docs/architecture-526","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#511-exception-handling-mechanisms","content":"Bounded output truncation"},"529":{"id":"/docs/architecture-527","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#511-exception-handling-mechanisms","content":"`core/bounded-output.ts`, `output-limits.ts`"},"530":{"id":"/docs/architecture-528","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#61-core-module-implementation","content":"**Composition root (`packages/unipi/index.ts`).** A single default-exported `ExtensionAPI` function. It creates the trajectory tracer, then for each module in the fixed order obtains `tracer.scope(name)` and invokes the module with the scoped proxy. Each module therefore sees a normal `ExtensionAPI`, but hook inputs/outputs are fingerprinted (`mutationSurface`, `mutationEvidence`) for later attribution."},"531":{"id":"/docs/architecture-529","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#61-core-module-implementation","content":"**`@pi-unipi/core` (\\~58 KB, zero internal dependencies).** `index.ts` re-exports `constants`, `events`, `sandbox`, `utils`, `model-cache`, `tui-overlay`, `tui-width`, `spinner-line`, `bounded-output`, and `fusion-status`. The two `Symbol.for` slots (`unipi.background-tasks.shared-registry`, `unipi.fusion.status`) are typed accessors that return `undefined` when the producer is absent, allowing consumers to degrade gracefully."},"532":{"id":"/docs/architecture-530","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#61-core-module-implementation","content":"**`subagents/tool-handler.ts`.** Routes on the `spawn_helper` payload's action family; resolves aliases and custom agents; enforces depth guard (children cannot see `spawn_helper`/`get_helper_result`), spawn and token budgets, and authority policy; shapes projected context; then hands to `AgentManager`. Foreground runs use the host's `createAgentSession` in-process; async runs spawn `pi --mode json -p` with a resolved binary (`UNIPI_SUBAGENT_PI_BINARY` override)."},"533":{"id":"/docs/architecture-531","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#61-core-module-implementation","content":"**`background-tasks/registry.ts` (`BackgroundTaskRegistry`).** Spawns child processes with `UNIPI_BG_*` env, tails stdout, recognises XML usage blocks and normalises them into a uniform usage record (model, context, tokens, tools), persists periodic snapshots, and exposes `allTasks()` synchronously through the shared symbol for the footer's 1-second refresh."},"534":{"id":"/docs/architecture-532","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#61-core-module-implementation","content":"**`mcp/bridge/*`.** `McpClient` implements JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio (`initialize`, `tools/list`, `tools/call`). `translator.ts` maps JSON Schema tool inputs to TypeBox-compatible Pi tool definitions and derives deterministic unique names. `ServerRegistry` owns start/stop/restart and emits `MCP_SERVER_*`/`MCP_TOOLS_*` events."},"535":{"id":"/docs/architecture-533","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#61-core-module-implementation","content":"**`memory/mempalace.ts`.** Invokes `bridge/mempalace_bridge.py` via `spawnSync`, exchanging one JSON line per operation. Auto-installs MemPalace through `uv`, caches the availability ping for 24 hours, and runs one-time migrations from legacy SQLite/markdown (`scripts/migrate-unipi-memory-to-mempalace.py`)."},"536":{"id":"/docs/architecture-534","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#62-key-algorithm-design","content":"**Deterministic compaction pipeline (`compile()`).**"},"537":{"id":"/docs/architecture-535","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#62-key-algorithm-design","content":"`normalize` — canonicalise message shapes and roles."},"538":{"id":"/docs/architecture-536","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#62-key-algorithm-design","content":"`filterNoise` — drop tool chatter, repeated status lines, and low-value turns."},"539":{"id":"/docs/architecture-537","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#62-key-algorithm-design","content":"`buildSections` — run extractors (`commits`, `files`, `goals`, `preferences`) to produce structured sections."},"540":{"id":"/docs/architecture-538","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#62-key-algorithm-design","content":"*(optional)* `selectRankedBriefBlocks` — rank blocks and select within budget."},"541":{"id":"/docs/architecture-539","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#62-key-algorithm-design","content":"`formatSummary` — render sections into the summary format."},"542":{"id":"/docs/architecture-540","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#62-key-algorithm-design","content":"`merge` — combine with the previous summary so knowledge accumulates across compactions."},"543":{"id":"/docs/architecture-541","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#62-key-algorithm-design","content":"Because no stage calls a model, the pipeline's cost is linear in message count, making `auto-trigger`'s per-turn evaluation (`token-estimate` vs configured budget) affordable."},"544":{"id":"/docs/architecture-542","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#62-key-algorithm-design","content":"**Depth and budget guard (subagents).** Nesting depth is bounded by excluding orchestration tools from child tool sets, so depth is structurally ≤ 1 for helpers; spawn and token budgets are checked before any process is created."},"545":{"id":"/docs/architecture-543","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#62-key-algorithm-design","content":"**Crash-safe artifact commit.** Write to `name.tmp` → `fsync` → atomic `rename` to final path → update versioned manifest. A crash at any point leaves either the previous or the new consistent state, never a torn file."},"546":{"id":"/docs/architecture-544","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#62-key-algorithm-design","content":"**Deterministic MCP tool naming.** Server identifier + tool name are combined into a stable, unique Pi tool name so registration is idempotent across restarts and collisions between servers are impossible."},"547":{"id":"/docs/architecture-545","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#62-key-algorithm-design","content":"**Responsive footer layout.** `FooterRenderer` computes a two-row layout from measured widths (`core/tui-width`), applies segment priorities and overflow handling, and repaints on a 1-second timer plus event triggers; `tps-tracker` computes tokens-per-second from streaming events."},"548":{"id":"/docs/architecture-546","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#62-key-algorithm-design","content":"**Kanboard parser auto-detection.** `ParserRegistry` selects a parser by file path pattern (plans, milestones, generic checkbox configs), then parses frontmatter and checkbox items into board columns."},"549":{"id":"/docs/architecture-547","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#63-data-structure-design","content":"Structure"},"550":{"id":"/docs/architecture-548","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#63-data-structure-design","content":"Definition"},"551":{"id":"/docs/architecture-549","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#63-data-structure-design","content":"Notes"},"552":{"id":"/docs/architecture-550","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#63-data-structure-design","content":"`UnipiEventPayload`"},"553":{"id":"/docs/architecture-551","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#63-data-structure-design","content":"Discriminated union of \\~22 payload interfaces in `core/events.ts`"},"554":{"id":"/docs/architect