ces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/boundary-interfaces#inter-module-events","content":"Inter-module events"},"934":{"id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces-36","page_id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/boundary-interfaces#kanboard-local-web-ui","content":"Kanboard local web UI"},"935":{"id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces-37","page_id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/boundary-interfaces","content":"This document describes the system's external invocation interfaces, including CLI commands, API endpoints, configuration parameters, and other boundary mechanisms."},"936":{"id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces-38","page_id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/boundary-interfaces#pi-extension-activation-default-export","content":"**Description**: Every @pi-unipi/\\* package exposes a default `(pi: ExtensionAPI) => void | Promise<void>` activation function referenced by the package.json `main` field. The Pi coding agent host loads the package, calls this function, and the package registers tools, slash commands, hooks and TUI widgets. There is no standalone binary; the startup surface is the extension loader plus configuration files and environment variables."},"937":{"id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces-39","page_id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/boundary-interfaces#pi-extension-activation-default-export","content":"**Source File**: `./packages/*/index.ts, ./packages/*/src/index.ts`"},"938":{"id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces-40","page_id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/boundary-interfaces#pi-extension-activation-default-export","content":"**Arguments**:"},"939":{"id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces-41","page_id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/boundary-interfaces#pi-extension-activation-default-export","content":"`pi` (ExtensionAPI): required - Host-provided ExtensionAPI instance used to register tools, commands, hooks and UI."},"940":{"id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces-42","page_id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/boundary-interfaces#pi-extension-activation-default-export","content":"**Options**:"},"941":{"id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces-43","page_id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/boundary-interfaces#pi-extension-activation-default-export","content":"`~/.unipi/config/<module>.json`(json file): optional - Global per-module configuration file (e.g. background-tasks.json, subagents.json, compactor). Loaded and validated at activation; missing files are scaffolded with defaults where supported. (default: `module defaults`)"},"942":{"id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces-44","page_id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/boundary-interfaces#pi-extension-activation-default-export","content":"`<cwd>/.unipi/config/<module>.json`(json file): optional - Workspace-level configuration override. Deep-merged over the global layer, workspace values win."},"943":{"id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces-45","page_id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/boundary-interfaces#pi-extension-activation-default-export","content":"**Usage Examples**:"},"944":{"id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces-46","page_id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/boundary-interfaces#unipimodel","content":"**Description**: Opens the fusion model picker TUI overlay. Lets the user select a lead/sidekick model pair from the Pi model registry, applies the result to the persisted FusionPreset, spawns the sidekick runtime and publishes session status (active pair, savings). Also injects itself as the first suggestion of the built-in `/model` autocomplete."},"945":{"id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces-47","page_id":"/docs/boundary-interfaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/boundary-interfaces#unipimodel","content":"**Source File**: `./packages/fusion/src/index.ts`"},"946":{"id":