,"1353":{"id":"/docs/overview-173","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#41-external-system-inventory","content":"**Notification platforms**"},"1354":{"id":"/docs/overview-174","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#41-external-system-inventory","content":"Native desktop, ntfy, gotify, Telegram, focus"},"1355":{"id":"/docs/overview-175","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#41-external-system-inventory","content":"Outbound notification dispatch"},"1356":{"id":"/docs/overview-176","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#41-external-system-inventory","content":"`notify`"},"1357":{"id":"/docs/overview-177","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#41-external-system-inventory","content":"**Operating system process and file systems**"},"1358":{"id":"/docs/overview-178","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#41-external-system-inventory","content":"Child process spawning and tree termination (incl. Windows `taskkill`), atomic file writes for artifacts"},"1359":{"id":"/docs/overview-179","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#41-external-system-inventory","content":"OS process control and filesystem"},"1360":{"id":"/docs/overview-180","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#41-external-system-inventory","content":"`background-tasks`, `subagents`, `mcp`, `fusion`"},"1361":{"id":"/docs/overview-181","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#41-external-system-inventory","content":"**Web browser (kanban board viewer)**"},"1362":{"id":"/docs/overview-182","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#41-external-system-inventory","content":"Consumer of the kanboard HTTP UI"},"1363":{"id":"/docs/overview-183","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#41-external-system-inventory","content":"HTTP (server-rendered pages)"},"1364":{"id":"/docs/overview-184","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#41-external-system-inventory","content":"`kanboard`"},"1365":{"id":"/docs/overview-185","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#42-interaction-descriptions","content":"**Pi coding agent (host).** This is the single most important relationship: Unipi has no runtime without Pi. Packages register tools with TypeBox schemas, slash commands (e.g. `/unipi compact`, `/unipi:model`, `/unipi:ralph`), hooks (compaction, lifecycle, milestone), and TUI overlays. The footer package drives Pi's `setFooter`/`setWidget` APIs, and the fusion, image and compactor packages consume Pi's model registry. Pi lifecycle events feed the notify package."},"1366":{"id":"/docs/overview-186","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#42-interaction-descriptions","content":"**MCP servers.** `ServerRegistry` loads server configuration, starts each configured server as a child process, and `McpClient` performs the `initialize` handshake and `listTools` over stdio. The translator converts MCP tool definitions into Pi-compatible schemas with unique names and registers them. Partial failures are cleaned up so one broken server does not block others. Agent tool calls are proxied back to the owning server via `callTool`."},"1367":{"id":"/docs/overview-187","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#42-interaction-descriptions","content":"**LLM and image model providers.** Unipi never talks to providers directly for chat; it resolves models through Pi's registry (cached in `core/model-cache`). The image package additionally includes an OpenAI-images-style API client and a chat-provider-to-images bridge, with vision gating based on the active model."},"1368":{"id":"/docs/overview-188","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#42-interaction-descriptions","content":"**MemPalace and SQLite.** Memory uses MemPalace as its primary backend through a Python bridge, with a markdown durable tier and migration from legacy SQLite. The compactor's `SessionDB` uses SQLite for per-project events, sessions and compaction counters, including schema migration."},"1369":{"id":"/docs/overview-189","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#42-interaction-descriptions","content":"**Web fetch stack.** The extraction pipeline validates URLs, fetches via `wreq-js` (TLS fingerprinting), routes by content type, extracts with `defuddle` and fallbacks, detects meta-refresh, and caches results. Search dispatch goes through a provider registry selectable via a TUI."},"1370":{"id":"/docs/overview-190","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#42-interaction-descriptions","content":"**Notification platforms.** Notify subscribes to Pi lifecycle events and to feature events discovered dynamically via `MODULE_READY` (task completion, ralph loop start/end, ask-user prompts), builds message text with priority mapping and recap summarization, and dispatches to whichever platforms are enabled."},"1371":{"id":"/docs/overview-191","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#42-interaction-descriptions","content":"**Operating system.** Background tasks and subagents spawn child Pi processes, tail output, parse usage payloads, persist snapshots and terminate process trees. The `DelegateArtifactStore` writes seed/prompt/result artifacts with crash-safe atomic writes and manifests."},"1372":{"id":"/docs/overview-192","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#43-dependency-analysis","content":"Dependency"},"1373":{"id":"/docs/overview-193","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#43-dependency-analysis","content":"Direction"},"1374":{"id":"/docs/overview-194","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#43-dependency-analysis","content":"Criticality"},"1375":{"id":"/docs/overview-195","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#43-dependency-analysis","content":"Failure impact"},"1376":{"id":"/docs/overview-196","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#43-dependency-analysis","content":"Pi coding agent"},"1377":{"id":"/docs/overview-197","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#43-dependency-analysis","content":"Unipi → Pi"},"1378":{"id":"/docs/overview-198","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#43-dependency-analysis","content":"Critical"},"1379":{"id":"/docs/overview-199","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#43-dependency-analysis","content":"Unipi cannot load or run at all."},"1380":{"id":"/docs/overview-200","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#43-dependency-analysis","content":"OS process/filesystem"},"1381":{"id":"/docs/overview-201","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#43-dependency-analysis","content":"Unipi → OS"},"1382":{"id":"/docs/overview-202","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#43-dependency-analysis","content":"Critical for orchestration"},"1383":{"id":"/docs/overview-203","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#43-dependency-analysis","content":"Subagents, background tasks, MCP servers and sidekick runtime unavailable."},"1384":{"id":"/docs/overview-204","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#43-dependency-analysis","content":"SQLite"},"1385":{"id":"/docs/overview-205","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#43-dependency-analysis","content":"Unipi → SQLite"},"1386":{"id":"/docs/overview-