ile the SystemContext level treats Unipi as a single box, the domain analysis reveals six internal domains connected through the core kernel. This view is provided to orient readers toward the Container level."},"1409":{"id":"/docs/overview-229","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#53-key-interaction-flows","content":"The following flows are ranked by importance in the domain analysis and illustrate how external systems participate."},"1410":{"id":"/docs/overview-230","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#flow-2--context-compaction-and-session-recall-importance-90","content":"A compaction hook, the `/unipi compact` command or the auto-trigger fires; the auto-trigger compares the token estimate against the budget (`compactor/src/compaction/auto-trigger.ts`)."},"1411":{"id":"/docs/overview-231","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#flow-2--context-compaction-and-session-recall-importance-90","content":"`compile()` runs the six-stage pipeline: normalize → filterNoise → buildSections → formatSummary → merge, optionally producing a ranked brief."},"1412":{"id":"/docs/overview-232","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#flow-2--context-compaction-and-session-recall-importance-90","content":"`SessionDB` records events and compaction counters in SQLite."},"1413":{"id":"/docs/overview-233","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#flow-2--context-compaction-and-session-recall-importance-90","content":"The compactor footer segment displays compaction statistics."},"1414":{"id":"/docs/overview-234","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#flow-2--context-compaction-and-session-recall-importance-90","content":"On resume, `resume-inject` and the `session_recall` tool restore prior context."},"1415":{"id":"/docs/overview-235","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#flow-3--mcp-server-tool-bridging-importance-80","content":"Configuration is loaded and synced (`mcp/src/config/manager.ts`)."},"1416":{"id":"/docs/overview-236","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#flow-3--mcp-server-tool-bridging-importance-80","content":"`ServerRegistry` prepares and starts servers, handling partial failures."},"1417":{"id":"/docs/overview-237","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#flow-3--mcp-server-tool-bridging-importance-80","content":"`McpClient` performs the initialize handshake and `listTools` over stdio."},"1418":{"id":"/docs/overview-238","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#flow-3--mcp-server-tool-bridging-importance-80","content":"The translator converts tools and registers them with Pi's `ExtensionAPI`."},"1419":{"id":"/docs/overview-239","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#flow-3--mcp-server-tool-bridging-importance-80","content":"The MCP footer segment shows active server and tool counts."},"1420":{"id":"/docs/overview-240","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#flow-4--web-smart-fetch-importance-65","content":"Tool invoked → provider selected from registry → URL validated, fetched via `wreq-js`, content-type routed, extracted with `defuddle` and fallbacks → result formatted and cached."},"1421":{"id":"/docs/overview-241","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#flow-5--model-fusion-preset-importance-65","content":"`/unipi:model` → model registry resolved, picker overlay mounted → preset persisted, sidekick runtime spawned → fusion status (active pair, savings) published through core → footer core segment renders it."},"1422":{"id":"/docs/overview-242","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#flow-6--structured-workflow-with-kanban-board-importance-60","content":"Workflow comman