"/docs/overview-278","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#61-technology-stack","content":"JSON-RPC over stdio (MCP), HTTP/HTTPS (web providers, notification platforms, kanboard UI)"},"1459":{"id":"/docs/overview-279","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#61-technology-stack","content":"Web extraction"},"1460":{"id":"/docs/overview-280","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#61-technology-stack","content":"`wreq-js` (TLS-fingerprinted fetch), `defuddle` (content extraction)"},"1461":{"id":"/docs/overview-281","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#61-technology-stack","content":"Process control"},"1462":{"id":"/docs/overview-282","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#61-technology-stack","content":"Node child processes, Windows `taskkill` tree termination, worktree isolation for subagents"},"1463":{"id":"/docs/overview-283","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#61-technology-stack","content":"Build tooling"},"1464":{"id":"/docs/overview-284","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#61-technology-stack","content":"Bundle build and dependency pin sync scripts (`scripts/build-bundle.mjs`, `scripts/sync-pins.mjs`)"},"1465":{"id":"/docs/overview-285","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#62-architecture-patterns","content":"**Plugin / microkernel.** `@pi-unipi/core` is the kernel; all other packages are plugins that register with the host and discover one another through events. The umbrella `@pi-unipi/unipi` package composes them."},"1466":{"id":"/docs/overview-286","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#62-architecture-patterns","content":"**Event-driven integration.** Cross-domain coupling is deliberately loose — the presentation domain (footer, notify) subscribes to events from orchestration, context and integration domains rather than importing their internals."},"1467":{"id":"/docs/overview-287","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#62-architecture-patterns","content":"**Registry pattern.** Recurs throughout: background-task registry, MCP `ServerRegistry`, web provider registry, footer segment registry, notify event-subscription registry, kanboard `ParserRegistry`, info-screen registry."},"1468":{"id":"/docs/overview-288","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#62-architecture-patterns","content":"**Pipeline pattern.** Compaction `compile()` and web `extract()` are explicit staged pipelines with well-defined intermediate representations."},"1469":{"id":"/docs/overview-289","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#62-architecture-patterns","content":"**Policy objects.** Subagent spawning applies budgets, depth guards, context policy and authority policy as separable libraries; the compactor's sandbox executor is guarded by a security policy scanner/evaluator."},"1470":{"id":"/docs/overview-290","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#62-architecture-patterns","content":"**Durable, crash-safe state.** `DelegateArtifactStore` and `durable-fs` provide atomic writes and manifests so process crashes do not corrupt artifacts."},"1471":{"id":"/docs/overview-291","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#63-key-design-decisions-and-observations","content":"**Complexity concentration.** Although coupling between domains is low, complexity inside a few hub files is high: `background-tasks/src/registry.ts`, `subagents/src/tool-handler.ts`, `compactor/src/compaction/summarize.ts` and `tools/register.ts`, `mcp/src/bridge/registry.ts`, and `web-api/src/engine/extract.ts`. These are the natural focus points for review and testing."},"1472":{"id":"/docs/overview-292","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#63-key-design-decisions-and-observations","content":"**Domain placement versus documentation.** Product documentation groups \"structured development\" as workflow/kanboard/milestone/trajectory/ralph. In code, `ralph` behaves as orchestration (iterative loops emitting loop events) and `trajectory` as context capture; this document places them with Agent Orchestration and Context & Memory Management respectively. Readers reconciling with earlier documentation should note this refinement."},"1473":{"id":"/docs/overview-293","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#63-key-design-decisions-and-observations","content":"**Cross-package coupling to watch.** `kanboard/parser` imports `milestone` types directly (strength 7.0 in the domain analysis). This is the strongest direct inter-package dependency outside the core kernel and is worth monitoring if the milestone model evolves."},"1474":{"id":"/docs/overview-294","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#63-key-design-decisions-and-observations","content":"**Configuration gating.** Every package is independently enableable, which supports incremental adoption but means the effective system context varies per installation — e.g. notify, kanboard's HTTP server or MCP bridging may be absent."},"1475":{"id":"/docs/overview-295","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#63-key-design-decisions-and-observations","content":"**Platform specifics.** Windows process-tree termination is handled explicitly (`windows-taskkill.ts`); the memory package depends on a Python runtime for the MemPalace bridge. Both are environmental prerequisites that sit at the system boundary."},"1476":{"id":"/docs/overview-296","page_id":"/docs/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/overview#64-summary","content":"Unipi occupies a clear position in its environment: it lives entirely inside the Pi coding agent as a family of loosely coupled extensions, and it reaches outward to MCP servers, model providers, web content, notification platforms and the operating system to make the agent more capable and its sessions longer. Its boundary is the set of `@pi-unipi/*` packages plus the local state they persist; everything it hosts, bridges or notifies is external. The core kernel and event bus are the architectural linchpin, and the next level of documentation (Container view) should elaborate the six internal domains and their hub components identified here."},"1477":{"id":"/docs/workflow","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"page","content":"Workflow","breadcrumbs":["Documentation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow"},"1478":{"id":"/docs/workflow-0","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow#1-workflow-overview","content":"1\\. Workflow Overview"},"1479":{"id":"/docs/workflow-1","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow#11-system-positioning","content":"1.1 System Positioning"},"1480":{"id":"/docs/workflow-2","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow#12-main-workflows","content":"1.2 Main Workflows"},"1481":{"id":"/docs/workflow-3","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow#13-core-execution-paths","content":"1.3 Core Execution Paths"},"1482":{"id":"/docs/workflow-4","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow#14-key-process-nodes","content":"1.4 Key Process Nodes"},"1483":{"id":"/docs/workflow-5","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow#15-process-coordination-mechanisms","content":"1.5 Process Coordination Mechanisms"},"1484":{"id":"/docs/workflow-6","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow#2-main-workflows","content":"2\\. Main Workflows"},"1485":{"id":"/docs/workflow-7","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url"