ounts, compactor stats) rather than being pushed to."},"1622":{"id":"/docs/workflow-144","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#15-process-coordination-mechanisms","content":"**Filesystem contracts** — `status.json`, `result.json`, `manifest.json`, `seed.json` in well-known directories allow the parent, child, and later sessions to coordinate without a shared process."},"1623":{"id":"/docs/workflow-145","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#21-w1--subagent-delegation-flow","content":"**Business purpose**: Let the primary agent fan out work to helper agents (foreground or background) while keeping its own context window bounded and enforcing guard rails against runaway spawning."},"1624":{"id":"/docs/workflow-146","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#211-top-level-routing","content":"`handleSpawnHelper` in `tool-handler.ts` never throws; it wraps every branch in a `try/catch` and returns a text result with `{ status: \"error\" }` on failure. Routing order is fixed:"},"1625":{"id":"/docs/workflow-147","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#211-top-level-routing","content":"`args.action` present → **management action** (`handleAction`)"},"1626":{"id":"/docs/workflow-148","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#211-top-level-routing","content":"`args.workflowScript` present → **workflow script** (`handleWorkflowScript`, or `handleAsyncWorkflowScript` for process-backed children)"},"1627":{"id":"/docs/workflow-149","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#211-top-level-routing","content":"otherwise → **single-child launch** (`handleSingleChild`)"},"1628":{"id":"/docs/workflow-150","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"`preflight()` executes the full validation chain *before* any process is created:"},"1629":{"id":"/docs/workflow-151","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"Check"},"1630":{"id":"/docs/workflow-152","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"Implementation"},"1631":{"id":"/docs/workflow-153","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"Failure message (visible to LLM)"},"1632":{"id":"/docs/workflow-154","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"Agent name present"},"1633":{"id":"/docs/workflow-155","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"`args.agent ?? args.type`"},"1634":{"id":"/docs/workflow-156","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"\"spawn\\_helper requires an agent (or legacy type) parameter.\""},"1635":{"id":"/docs/workflow-157","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"Alias resolution"},"1636":{"id":"/docs/workflow-158","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"`manager.resolveAlias()` → `manager.getAgentConfig()`"},"1637":{"id":"/docs/workflow-159","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"\"Unknown agent type … Known types: …\""},"1638":{"id":"/docs/workflow-160","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"Enablement"},"1639":{"id":"/docs/workflow-161","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"`manager.isTypeEnabled()`"},"1640":{"id":"/docs/workflow-162","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"\"Agent type … is disabled by configuration.\""},"1641":{"id":"/docs/workflow-163","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"Depth guard"},"1642":{"id":"/docs/workflow-164","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"`resolveMaxSubagentDepth()` + `depthExceeded(env, maxDepth)` (depth carried in child env)"},"1643":{"id":"/docs/workflow-165","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"\"Subagent depth cap reached (maxSubagentDepth N)…\""},"1644":{"id":"/docs/workflow-166","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"Prompt present"},"1645":{"id":"/docs/workflow-167","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"`args.task ?? args.prompt`"},"1646":{"id":"/docs/workflow-168","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"\"spawn\\_helper requires a task (or legacy prompt) parameter.\""},"1647":{"id":"/docs/workflow-169","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"Post-preflight, `handleSingleChild` applies:"},"1648":{"id":"/docs/workflow-170","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"**Context policy**: explicit `context: \"fork\"` never silently downgrades — it requires background mode *and* the process runner; otherwise a typed error is returned."},"1649":{"id":"/docs/workflow-171","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"**Budgets**: turn budget (appended to the child system prompt via `appendTurnBudgetSystemPrompt`), tool budget, usage budget."},"1650":{"id":"/docs/workflow-172","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"**Acceptance gates**: `gate` shorthand (single verify command) is mutually exclusive with the `acceptance` object."},"1651":{"id":"/docs/workflow-173","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#212-preflight-gating-guard-rails-before-side-effects","content":"**Session spawn budget**: `spawnAccounting.used() >= cap` → refuse with guidance to use `grant-spawn-budget` from the interactive root session."},"1652":{"id":"/docs/workflow-174","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#213-background-process-mode-execution-path","content":"When `runAsync` is chosen, `runAsyncSubagent` in `async-runner.ts` executes the child with a strict status lifecycle recorded in `status.json`:"},"1653":{"id":"/docs/workflow-175","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#213-background-process-mode-execution-path","content":"Key implementation properties observed in `runChildProcess`:"},"1654":{"id":"/docs/workflow-176","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#213-background-process-mode-execution-path","content":"**Process-group kill**: `trySignalChild` sends the signal to `-child.pid` (the detached process group) so grandchild shells are terminated too, falling back to `child.kill()`."},"1655":{"id":"/docs/workflow-177","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#213-background-process-mode-execution-path","content":"**Terminal proof**: `pid`, `exitCode`, and `signal` are recorded on the result so the parent can distinguish a real exit from a lost child."},"1656":{"id":"/docs/workflow-178","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#213-background-process-mode-execution-path","content":"**Usage extraction**: tolerant to both `input/output/total` and `inputTokens/outputTokens/totalTokens` field naming."},"1657":{"id":"/docs/workflow-179","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#213-background-process-mode-execution-path","content":"**stderr heuristics**: the last three lines matching `/Error|FATAL/i` are captured (≤500 chars) as the error string for non-zero exits."},"1658":{"id":"/docs/workflow-180","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#214-durable-delegate-launch-background-tasks-delegate-subsystem","content":"For registry-managed delegates (`bg_delegate`), `prepareDelegateLaunch` in `delegate/runner.ts` enforces an ordering guarantee: **preflight refusals create nothing**."},"1659":{"id":"/docs/workflow-181","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#214-durable-delegate-launch-background-tasks-delegate-subsystem","content":"Route pinning (`resolveDelegateRoute` in `launch.ts`) has **no fallback**: an unavailable provider/model pair is a typed `route_unresolved` refusal, because silently answering on a different model is treated as a correctness failure."},"1660":{"id":"/docs/workflow-182","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#215-result-retrieval-and-delivery","content":"`get_helper_result` reads the committed result and applies `truncateOutput` (reference default 200 KB / 5000 lines via `resolveMaxOutput`)."},"1661":{"id":"/docs/workflow-183","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#215-result-retrieval-and-delivery","content":"For delegates, `decideDelegateDelivery(answerBytes, requested, cap)` chooses `inline` when the exact serialized answer is within `DELEGATE_INLINE_ANSWER_BYTES`, otherwise degrades explicitly to an **artifact reference** — the answer is never shortened to fit. Requesting inline for an oversized answer raises `result_too_large_for_inline` with remediation steps."},"1662":{"id":"/docs/workflow-184","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#22-w2--context-compaction--session-recall-flow","content":"**Business purpose**: Keep long sessions viable by replacing raw history with a deterministic, zero-LLM structured summary, while persisting statistics and enabling recall."},"1663":{"id":"/docs/workflow-185","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#221-trigger-sources","content":"Source"},"1664":{"id":"/docs/workflow-186","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#221-trigger-sources","content":"Path"},"1665":{"id":"/docs/workflow-187","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#221-trigger-sources","content":"Pi's own threshold/overflow compaction"},"1666":{"id":"/docs/workflow-188","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#221-trigger-sources","content":"Pi emits `session_before_compact` with \\`reason: \"threshold\""},"1667":{"id":"/docs/workflow-189","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#221-trigger-sources","content":"\"overflow\"`; compactor intercepts only if `config.overrideDefaultCompaction\\` is true"},"1668":{"id":"/docs/workflow-190","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#221-trigger-sources","content":"`/unipi:compact` or `compact` tool"},"1669":{"id":"/docs/workflow-191","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#221-trigger-sources","content":"Custom instructions carry the compactor marker (`isCompactor`) and optional `keep:N` / follow-up prompt"},"1670":{"id":"/docs/workflow-192","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#221-trigger-sources","content":"UniPi auto-compaction"},"1671":{"id":"/docs/workflow-193","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#221-trigger-sources","content":"`decideAutoCompaction()` evaluates a context-usage sample and, when it fires, calls `ctx.compact()`"},"1672":{"id":"/docs/workflow-194","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#222-auto-trigger-decision-algorithm","content":"`decideAutoCompaction` is a **pure function** over `(config, usage, state, nowMs)` returning `{ shouldTrigger, reason, state }`. Its decision order embeds loop safeguards:"},"1673":{"id":"/docs/workflow-195","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#222-auto-trigger-decision-algorithm","content":"Defaults (`AUTO_COMPACTION_DEFAULTS`): disabled, threshold 80 %, cooldown 60 s, repeat growth 4 000 tokens, notify on. Values are clamped (`thresholdPercent` 1–99, `cooldownMs` ≤ 24 h)."},"1674":{"id":"/docs/workflow-196","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#222-auto-trigger-decision-algorithm","content":"State transitions after a trigger: `markAutoCompactionComplete` sets `inFlight=false, awaitingPostCompactionSample=true`; `markAutoCompactionError` clears in-flight but keeps `lastTriggerAt` so cooldown still applies."},"1675":{"id":"/docs/workflow-197","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#224-the-compile-pipeline-summarizets","content":"`compile()` — unranked path, caps the brief transcript."},"1676":{"id":"/docs/workflow-198","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#224-the-compile-pipeline-summarizets","content":"`compileRanked()` — used by the hook; passes `briefBlocksFor = selectRankedBriefBlocks(...)`, disables the fresh-brief cap and preserves the fresh brief on merge."},"1677":{"id":"/docs/workflow-199","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#224-the-compile-pipeline-summarizets","content":"`mergePrevious` first strips the previous summary's `RECALL_NOTE` (`stripRecallNote`) so the note is never duplicated."},"1678":{"id":"/docs/workflow-200","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#224-the-compile-pipeline-summarizets","content":"The budget is **char-based but token-calibrated**: `maxBriefChars = 1100 × charsPerToken` where `charsPerToken` comes from Pi's real `tokensBefore`."},"1679":{"id":"/docs/workflow-201","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#225-post-compaction-session_compact","content":"Ignored unless `event.fromExtension` and not already handled by `/unipi:compact`'s own toast."},"1680":{"id":"/docs/workflow-202","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#225-post-compaction-session_compact","content":"If `willRetry`, nothing is shown."},"1681":{"id":"/docs/workflow-203","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#225-post-compaction-session_compact","content":"Toast via `formatCompactionStats(stats)` after 500 ms."},"1682":{"id":"/docs/workflow-204","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#225-post-compaction-session_compact","content":"If a `followUpPrompt` was parsed, it is sent as a user message; otherwise, for threshold/overflow reasons with `continueAfterThresholdCompact`, an **invisible auto-continue** is scheduled: a `custom` message with `customType: \"compactor-auto-continue\"`, `display: false`, `triggerTurn: true`, `deliverAs: \"followUp\"`. The `context` hook filters that message out of the LLM payload so the model simply continues from the summary."},"1683":{"id":"/docs/workflow-205","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#226-persistence-and-recall","content":"`SessionDB` (`session/db.ts`) is project-scoped SQLite with worktree/hash suffix handling, schema migrations, and pre-prepared statements; it records events, session metadata, and cumulative compaction counters."},"1684":{"id":"/docs/workflow-206","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#226-persistence-and-recall","content":"On `session_start`, `resume-inject` re-injects the prior summary; the `session_recall` tool pulls specific recall blocks on demand."},"1685":{"id":"/docs/workflow-207","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#226-persistence-and-recall","content":"The footer compactor segment reads live Pi session data (the `COMPACTOR_STATS_UPDATED` event is retained only for compatibility)."},"1686":{"id":"/docs/workflow-208","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#23-w3--mcp-server-tool-bridging-flow","content":"**Business purpose**: Turn external MCP servers into ordinary Pi tools with deterministic naming and clean failure semantics."},"1687":{"id":"/docs/workflow-209","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#231-startup-with-a-discovery-barrier","content":"`ServerRegistry.startServers()` prepares all servers **in parallel** and registers tools only after **every** server has either prepared or failed:"},"1688":{"id":"/docs/workflow-210","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#233-failure-semantics","content":"Any single server failing does **not** block others; its entry stays in `error` state with the message and an `MCP_SERVER_ERROR` event is emitted."},"1689":{"id":"/docs/workflow-211","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#233-failure-semantics","content":"Duplicate *final* tool names across servers fail the whole batch: `failPreparedServers` disconnects all prepared clients before rethrowing."},"1690":{"id":"/docs/workflow-212","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#233-failure-semantics","content":"If `registerTool` throws mid-batch and the host supports unregistration, already-registered names are rolled back in reverse order; on Pi 0.80 (no rollback) the partial set is **kept and reported truthfully** with the message \"some MCP tools remain registered until Pi restarts\"."},"1691":{"id":"/docs/workflow-213","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#233-failure-semantics","content":"`stopServer` refuses to run when tools are registered but the host cannot unregister them, instructing the user to restart Pi."},"1692":{"id":"/docs/workflow-214","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#233-failure-semantics","content":"`disconnectAll` (extension shutdown) disconnects clients without claiming tools were removed."},"1693":{"id":"/docs/workflow-215","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#233-failure-semantics","content":"`McpClient` details: stderr is capped at 10 000 chars (trimmed to the last 5 000), exit during startup rejects with the stderr tail, and an unexpected exit after connection rejects all pending requests."},"1694":{"id":"/docs/workflow-216","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#24-w4--web-smart-fetch-flow","content":"**Business purpose**: Give the agent robust access to web content despite bot-detection and messy HTML."},"1695":{"id":"/docs/workflow-217","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#24-w4--web-smart-fetch-flow","content":"Error classification in the catch block: messages containing `timeout` → `timeout` (phase `waiting`, retryable); `network`/`ECONNREFUSED` → `network_error` (phase `connecting`, retryable); anything else → `unexpected_response` (not retryable). `createError` returns a **real `Error` instance** carrying the `FetchError` fields so boundary catches surface `.message` rather than `[object Object]`."},"1696":{"id":"/docs/workflow-218","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#24-w4--web-smart-fetch-flow","content":"**Batch fetch** (`defuddleFetchMultiple`) implements a bounded worker pool (`DEFAULT_BATCH_CONCURRENCY`): each worker pulls the next index on completion, results are written positionally, and per-item errors are captured rather than failing the batch. The return value reports `total`, `succeeded`, `failed`, and `items`."},"1697":{"id":"/docs/workflow-219","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#25-w5--model-fusion-preset-flow","content":"**Business purpose**: Pair a primary and a \"sidekick\" model to reduce cost while surfacing savings in the footer."},"1698":{"id":"/docs/workflow-220","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#25-w5--model-fusion-preset-flow","content":"Downstream effects: the active model pair influences vision gating in the image package and the savings telemetry (`savings.ts`) shown in the footer."},"1699":{"id":"/docs/workflow-221","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#26-w6--structured-workflow-with-kanban-board-flow","content":"**Business purpose**: Give teams disciplined, sandboxed development steps and a visual board generated from markdown artefacts."},"1700":{"id":"/docs/workflow-222","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#26-w6--structured-workflow-with-kanban-board-flow","content":"Note: `kanboard/parser` imports milestone types directly — the one hard intra-domain coupling in an otherwise event-driven system."},"1701":{"id":"/docs/workflow-223","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#27-w7--interactive-ask-user-flow","content":"**Business purpose**: Let the agent block for a human decision, optionally alerting a remote device and supporting hand-off to a fresh session."},"1702":{"id":"/docs/workflow-224","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#28-w8--notification-dispatch-flow-cross-cutting","content":"`registerEventListeners` in `notify/events.ts` distinguishes two subscription channels:"},"1703":{"id":"/docs/workflow-225","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#28-w8--notification-dispatch-flow-cross-cutting","content":"**Pi lifecycle hooks** (`agent_end`, `agent_settled`, `session_shutdown`) must use `pi.on()` — these are replaced automatically on reload."},"1704":{"id":"/docs/workflow-226","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#28-w8--notification-dispatch-flow-cross-cutting","content":"**Event-bus events** (`unipi:*`, third-party `rpiv:ask-user:prompt`, `permissions:ui_prompt`) use `pi.events.on()`; unsubscribe functions are collected in `unsubs` and `unregisterAll()` runs before each registration to prevent listener accumulation across reloads."},"1705":{"id":"/docs/workflow-227","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#28-w8--notification-dispatch-flow-cross-cutting","content":"Dispatch is **fire-and-forget** from the handler (`.catch(() => {})`) so a slow or failing platform never blocks the emitter. `hasPendingWakeTask()` reads the shared registry symbol to know whether a running background task will wake the agent, informing whether an \"input needed\" alert is warranted."},"1706":{"id":"/docs/workflow-228","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#29-w0--extension-bootstrap--module-discovery","content":"Operational implication: a missing tool or footer segment is usually a **configuration state**, not a defect — check the master toggle and whether `MODULE_READY` was emitted."},"1707":{"id