-recovery-mechanisms","content":"**Crash-safe persistence (delegate artifacts, `durable-fs.ts`)** — every artifact is written to a same-directory temporary file, fsynced, renamed into place, then the directory is fsynced on POSIX. A file under its final name is complete by construction; a crash or full disk cannot leave a truncated artifact that looks whole. `DurableFileError` records `operation`, `path`, `nativeCode`, `cleanupFailures`, and whether the rename completed."},"1832":{"id":"/docs/workflow-354","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#42-recovery-mechanisms","content":"**Zero-activity EDR retry (async runner)** — if the child is SIGKILLed with `code === null` before any stdout/stderr activity, the run is marked `retriedFileDelivery` and `runAsyncSubagent` retries **once** with `taskDelivery: \"file\"`, writing `retry: \"file-delivery\"` into `status.json`."},"1833":{"id":"/docs/workflow-355","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#42-recovery-mechanisms","content":"**Delegate terminal evaluation** — when `result.json` is missing, `evaluateDelegateTerminal` reads `child-terminal.json` for the child's own error code/message, lists preserved artifacts (`child-terminal.json`, `runtime-budget.json`, task output), and returns a failed/cancelled outcome with a diagnostic pointer. No partial answer is fabricated."},"1834":{"id":"/docs/workflow-356","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#42-recovery-mechanisms","content":"**Retained children / resume** — completed async runs are retained under the async dir; `spawn_helper { action: \"resume\", id, message }` relaunches the agent with `resumeSessionFile` so the stored session contract continues."},"1835":{"id":"/docs/workflow-357","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#42-recovery-mechanisms","content":"**Session recall** — after any process crash, `SessionDB` and `resume-inject` restore prior summaries on the next `session_start`."},"1836":{"id":"/docs/workflow-358","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#42-recovery-mechanisms","content":"**Auto-compaction error recovery** — `markAutoCompactionError` clears `inFlight` so a failed `ctx.compact()` cannot wedge the trigger, while preserving `lastTriggerAt` so cooldown still applies."},"1837":{"id":"/docs/workflow-359","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#43-fault-tolerance-strategy-design","content":"**Fail-closed before side effects** — subagent preflight, delegate preflight (`childCreated: false`), ask-user allow-list, MCP unique-name assertion, and URL validation all refuse before spawning, rendering, or fetching."},"1838":{"id":"/docs/workflow-360","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#43-fault-tolerance-strategy-design","content":"**Isolation of failure domains** — a failed MCP server, a failed notification platform, or a failed batch-fetch item never fails its siblings (`Promise.allSettled` / per-item try-catch)."},"1839":{"id":"/docs/workflow-361","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#43-fault-tolerance-strategy-design","content":"**Typed, remediable errors** — `DelegateError.code` (over 30 codes), `FetchError.code/phase/retryable`, and human-readable `remediation[]` lists let both the LLM and the operator act without reading logs."},"1840":{"id":"/docs/workflow-362","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#43-fault-tolerance-strategy-design","content":"**No silent substitution** — route pinning has no fallback; oversized delegate answers become artifact references rather than truncated text; MCP partial registrations are reported rather than hidden."},"1841":{"id":"/docs/workflow-363","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#43-fault-tolerance-strategy-design","content":"**Defensive event