gistry` for info-screen groups (`subagents` and `ralph` register groups)."},"2147":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/agent-orchestration-domain-179","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/agent-orchestration-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/agent-orchestration-domain#7-observations-and-considerations","content":"**Two parallel child-process orchestrators.** `subagents/async-runner.ts` and `background-tasks/registry.ts` both spawn `pi` children, both enforce timeouts and tree-kill, and both persist artifacts—but under different roots (`$TMPDIR/unipi-subagents-*` vs the background runtime dir / `.unipi/delegate`). They embody different trust models: subagents are configurable and may be write-capable; delegates are inspect-only, route-pinned, and hash-verified. Consolidating spawn/kill/artifact primitives into a shared module would reduce duplication without erasing that distinction."},"2148":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/agent-orchestration-domain-180","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/agent-orchestration-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/agent-orchestration-domain#7-observations-and-considerations","content":"**Hub concentration.** `tool-handler.ts` (\\~49 KB), `subagents/index.ts` (\\~45 KB) and `registry.ts` (\\~73 KB) centralize most decision logic. `registry.ts` in particular mixes process lifecycle, telemetry parsing, and persistence."},"2149":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/agent-orchestration-domain-181","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/agent-orchestration-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/agent-orchestration-domain#7-observations-and-considerations","content":"**Stale kernel metadata.** `core/constants.ts#MODULES` lacks a `BACKGROUND_TASKS` entry; subagents emits `MODULE_READY` with a hard-coded `version: \"0.2.0\"` rather than reading `package.json`."},"2150":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/agent-orchestration-domain-182","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/agent-orchestration-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/agent-orchestration-domain#7-observations-and-considerations","content":"**Implicit contracts worth preserving.** The `sessionEnded` latch ordering in `subagents/index.ts`, the \"preflight creates nothing\" property in `delegate/launch.ts`, and the \"result.json presence is the only success signal\" rule in `delegate/runner.ts` are all load-bearing invariants documented only in comments and tests; they should be kept in mind when modifying these paths."},"2151":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","type":"page","content":"Context & Memory Management","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Deep Exploration"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain"},"2152":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-0","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"1\\. Domain Overview"},"2153":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-1","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#11-position-in-the-overall-architecture","content":"1.1 Position in the overall architecture"},"2154":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-2","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#2-compactor-compaction-engine","content":"2\\. Compactor: Compaction Engine"},"2155":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-3","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deep-explorati