:"**Project:** Unipi (`@pi-unipi/*` extension suite for the Pi coding agent)\n&#x2A;*Packages covered:** `packages/compactor`, `packages/memory`, `packages/trajectory`\n&#x2A;*Document date:** 2026-09-16"},"2186":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-34","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"The Context & Memory Management domain is responsible for the scarcest resource in an agentic coding session: the model's context window. It provides three complementary capabilities, each implemented as an independently loadable extension package:"},"2187":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-35","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"Capability"},"2188":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-36","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"Package"},"2189":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-37","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"Core idea"},"2190":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-38","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"**Context compaction & session recall**"},"2191":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-39","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"`@pi-unipi/compactor`"},"2192":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-40","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"Replace raw conversation history with a compact, deterministic, structured summary — with zero LLM calls — and keep the discarded detail searchable."},"2193":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-41","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"**Persistent cross-session memory**"},"2194":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-42","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"`@pi-unipi/memory`"},"2195":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-43","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"Store durable facts (preferences, decisions, patterns, summaries) in a MemPalace backend with a human-readable markdown tier, scoped per project."},"2196":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-44","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"**Trajectory capture & observability**"},"2197":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-45","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"`@pi-unipi/trajectory`"},"2198":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-46","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"Record what every hook and API call did to the context, verify provider-request prefix integrity, and serve a live trajectory view."},"2199":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-47","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"Together they deliver the domain's value proposition: longer autonomous sessions with less manual context management, and continuity across sessions. All three packages depend only on `@pi-unipi/core` and integrate with the host through the Pi `ExtensionAPI` (tools, slash commands, lifecycle hooks)."},"2200":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-48","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#21-design-philosophy","content":"The compactor is a **deterministic, zero-LLM** summarizer. Rather than asking a model to summarize the conversation (slow, expensive, non-reproducible), it runs a chain of pure functions over normalized message blocks. Every stage takes `NormalizedBlock[]` or `SectionData` as input and returns a new value, so stages can be tested and recomposed independently. Because compaction is cheap, it can safely be auto-triggered on a percentage threshold."},"2201":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-49","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#21-design-philosophy","content":"The core data type (`src/types.ts`) is:"},"2202":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-50","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#21-design-philosophy","content":"The output of the pipeline is a bracketed text summary (`[Session Goal]`, `[Files And Changes]`, `[Commits]`, `[Outstanding Context]`, `[User Preferences]`) followed by a *brief transcript*, then a `RECALL_NOTE` telling the model it can retrieve dropped detail via the recall tool."},"2203":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-51","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`src/compaction/summarize.ts` is the orchestrator. It exposes two entry points sharing one implementation, `compileWithBriefBlocks`:"},"2204":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-52","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"**`compile(input)`** — the unranked path. The brief transcript is built from all filtered blocks and capped at `BRIEF_MAX_LINES = 120`."},"2205":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-53","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"**`compileRanked(input)`** — the path used by the live compaction hook. Blocks are first scored and selected under a character budget (`selectRankedBriefBlocks`), the fresh brief is **not** capped, and merging preserves the fresh brief (`preserveFreshBriefOnMerge: true`)."},"2206":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-54","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"**Stage 1 — Normalize.** `normalizeMessages` maps each pi-ai `Message` into `NormalizedBlock`s, extracting text from mixed content parts (`text`, `toolCall`, `thinking`) via `content.ts#textOf`. `sanitize.ts` strips control characters and normalizes whitespace."},"2207":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-55","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"**Stage 2 — Filter noise.** `filter-noise.ts` drops:"},"2208":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-56","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"all `thinking` blocks;"},"2209":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-57","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`tool_call`/`tool_result` blocks whose tool is in `NOISE_TOOLS` (`TodoWrite`, `TodoRead`, `ToolSearch`, `WebSearch`, `AskUser`, `ExitSpecMode`, `GenerateDroid`);"},"2210":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-58","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"user blocks containing `NOISE_STRINGS` (e.g. \"Continue from where you left off.\") or user-configured `customNoisePatterns`;"},"2211":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-59","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"XML wrappers such as `<system-reminder>`, `<ide_opened_file>`, `<command-message>`, `<context-window-usage>` (`XML_WRAPPER_RE`), and user blocks that become empty after stripping them."},"2212":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-60","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"**Stage 3 — Build sections.** `build-sections.ts` produces `SectionData` by running the heuristic extractors:"},"2213":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-61","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"Extractor"},"2214":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-62","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"Output section"},"2215":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-63","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"Notes"},"2216":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-64","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`extractGoals`"},"2217":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-65","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`[Session Goal]`"},"2218":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-66","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"Task-verb / scope-change regexes over user turns"},"2219":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-67","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`extractFiles` → `formatFileActivity`"},"2220":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-68","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`[Files And Changes]`"},"2221":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-69","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"Classifies paths into `Modified`, `Created`, `Read` sets; paths present in *Modified* are removed from *Created*; each category capped at 10 with `(+N more)`"},"2222":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-70","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`extractCommits` → `formatCommits`"},"2223":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-71","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`[Commits]`"},"2224":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-72","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"Commit hash + message detection"},"2225":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-73","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`extractOutstandingContext`"},"2226":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-74","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`[Outstanding Context]`"},"2227":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-75","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"Inspects the last 20 blocks for error tool results and `BLOCKER_RE` matches (\"failed\", \"broken\", \"blocked\", \"crash\"…); at most 5 items"},"2228":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-76","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`extractPreferences` → `dedupPreferencesAgainstGoals`"},"2229":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-77","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`[User Preferences]`"},"2230":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-78","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"Preferences that duplicate goals are dropped"},"2231":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-79","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`buildBriefSections` → `stringifyBrief`"},"2232":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-80","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"brief transcript"},"2233":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-81","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"Built from `briefBlocks` when supplied (ranked path), else all blocks"},"2234":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-82","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"**Stage 4 — Rank (ranked path only).** `rank.ts` scores each block by *signal density* and adds a `reasons[]` trail for debuggability. Representative weights: user turn +18, assistant +10, edit tool (`edit|write|multiedit|apply_patch…`) +34, test/build command (`TEST_COMMAND_RE`) +26, recency 0–12, tool result +1. Bash blocks consisting only of scaffolding (`set -e`, `cd`, `echo`, `ls`, heredoc bodies…) receive `TRIVIAL_BASH_PENALTY = 16`. Hook-provided `fileOps` (read/written/edited files reported by Pi) are used as a structural signal instead of prose guessing. Selection is governed by `BriefRankingOptions`:"},"2235":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-83","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`maxBlocks` (default 80) and `preserveRecentBlocks` (default 16) as safety bounds;"},"2236":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-84","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`maxBriefChars` (floor), `maxBriefCharsCeiling`, `briefCharsPerBlock` (slope) — a **size-relative budget**: `clamp(briefCharsPerBlock × blockCount, floor, ceiling)`, so long transcripts earn more brief budget while small sessions stay at the floor."},"2237":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-85","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`brief.ts#compileBrief` renders the selected blocks with per-segment head/tail word budgets, keeps heredoc commands intact (`heredocCloseIndex`), labels tool calls with an extracted path, and collapses `<skill name=…>` blocks (`skill-collapse.ts`)."},"2238":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-86","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"**Stage 5 — Format.** `format.ts#formatSummary` renders each non-empty section as `[Title]\\n- item…`, joins sections with `\\n\\n---\\n\\n`, and (for the unranked path) applies `capBrief`, which keeps the last 120 lines and prefixes `...(N earlier lines omitted)`."},"2239":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-87","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"**Stage 6 — Merge.** `merge.ts#mergePrevious` parses the previous summary by header (`sectionOf`) and merges section by section:"},"2240":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-88","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`Outstanding Context` is always replaced by the fresh version (blockers are transient);"},"2241":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-89","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"`Files And Changes` is merged set-wise per category (`mergeFileLines`), Modified wins over Created;"},"2242":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-90","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"other sections are de-duplicated line-wise and capped as a rolling window (`Session Goal` 8, `Commits` 8, others 15);"},"2243":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-91","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"the brief transcript is re-budgeted via `mergeBriefTranscriptWithFreshBudget`."},"2244":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-92","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#22-the-six-stage-compile-pipeline","content":"Before merging, `stripRecallNote` removes the previous `RECALL_NOTE` so it is not duplicated."},"2245":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-93","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#23-cut-selection-what-gets-summarized-vs-kept","content":"`src/compaction/cut.ts` decides the boundary between \"history to summarize\" and \"tail to keep verbatim\":"},"2246":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-94","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#23-cut-selection-what-gets-summarized-vs-kept","content":"`collectLiveMessages` walks the append-only branch, starts after the last `compaction` entry's `firstKeptEntryId`, and performs **orphan recovery** when that id is the `\"\"` sentinel (prior compact-all) or no longer exists in the branch. `custom_message` and `branch_summary` entries are converted to their agent-message form so they count as live context."},"2247":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-95","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#23-cut-selection-what-gets-summarized-vs-kept","content":"`buildOwnCut(branchEntries, keepUserTurns)` returns `OwnCutResult`: either `{ ok: true, messages, firstKeptEntryId, keptUserTurns, … }` or `{ ok: false, reason }` with `OwnCutCancelReason` = `no_live_messages` | `too_few_live_messages` (≤ 2 live messages)."},"2248":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-96","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#23-cut-selection-what-gets-summarized-vs-kept","content":"`resolveSmartKeepUserTurns` boosts the default `keep:1` to a larger tail when the tail is small (config `smartKeepTail`); an explicit `keep:N` from the user is always respected."},"2249":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-97","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#23-cut-selection-what-gets-summarized-vs-kept","content":"`applyTailBudget` rescues autonomous or oversized-tail sessions with a token-budget cut (`budgetCut: \"no_anchor\" | \"oversized_tail\"`), only on the default (non-explicit) path."},"2250":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-98","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#23-cut-selection-what-gets-summarized-vs-kept","content":"User intent arrives through `compact-args.ts#parseCompactionInstructions`: exactly `COMPACTOR_INSTRUCTION` (from core) selects the default path; `COMPACTOR_INSTRUCTION keep:N …` parses an explicit keep count; any other instruction is treated as \"not ours\" but still parsed for a trailing `keep:N` and follow-up prompt."},"2251":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-99","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#24-token-estimation-with-per-session-calibration","content":"`token-estimate.ts` is character-based, with `DEFAULT_CHARS_PER_TOKEN = 4` clamped to `[2, 6]`. At compaction time `hooks.ts` calibrates the ratio from Pi's *real* `preparation.tokensBefore` against the measured character count of live messages plus the previous summary (`calibrateCharsPerToken`), yielding `{ mode: \"heuristic\" | \"calibrated\", charsPerToken }`. `estimateMessageContentChars` counts every token-bearing part (text, thinking, tool call name + arguments, tool result content, images at `IMAGE_CONTENT_CHARS = 4800`) so the calibrated ratio is not deflated. The ranked brief budget (`RANKED_BRIEF_BUDGET_TOKENS = 1100`, ceiling `2000`, `15` tokens per block) is converted to characters using this calibrated ratio, so the summary targets a token size regardless of content density."},"2252":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-100","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#25-compaction-hooks-hooksts","content":"`registerCompactionHooks(pi, deps)` binds the engine into three Pi events:"},"2253":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-101","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#25-compaction-hooks-hooksts","content":"**`context`** — filters out the invisible auto-continue marker message (`customType === \"compactor-auto-continue\"`) from the LLM payload."},"2254":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-102","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#25-compaction-hooks-hooksts","content":"**`session_before_compact`** — the main path (see sequence below). It only acts when the instruction carries the compactor marker **or** `config.overrideDefaultCompaction` is true; otherwise it returns and lets Pi's native compaction proceed. On an unworkable cut during an `overflow` compaction it returns without cancelling so Pi core can retry; otherwise it returns `{ cancel: true }` with a UI warning."},"2255":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-103","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#25-compaction-hooks-hooksts","content":"**`session_compact`** — shows the post-compaction toast (`formatCompactionStats`), sends a pending follow-up prompt via `pi.sendUserMessage`, or, when `continueAfterThresholdCompact` is enabled and the reason was `threshold`/`overflow`, schedules `triggerInvisibleContinue`: a hidden custom message (`content: []`, `display: false`, `triggerTurn: true`, `deliverAs: \"followUp\"`) that makes the agent resume from the summary without polluting context."},"2256":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-104","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#25-compaction-hooks-hooksts","content":"`details` returned to Pi records `compactor: \"@pi-unipi/compactor\"`, the list of section headers, source message count, whether a previous summary was used, the compaction reason and any budget cut — useful when inspecting the session file."},"2257":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-105","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#26-auto-compaction-trigger-auto-triggerts","content":"`auto-trigger.ts` is a **pure state machine**: it never touches Pi, it only decides whether a context-usage sample should trigger compaction. State is immutable; every function returns a new `AutoCompactionState`."},"2258":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-106","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#26-auto-compaction-trigger-auto-triggerts","content":"Defaults (`AUTO_COMPACTION_DEFAULTS`): `enabled: false`, `thresholdPercent: 80`, `cooldownMs: 60 000`, `repeatMinGrowthTokens: 4 000`, `notify: true`. `normalizeAutoCompactionConfig` clamps threshold to `[1, 99]`, cooldown to `[0, 24h]`, growth to `[0, 10M]`."},"2259":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-107","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#26-auto-compaction-trigger-auto-triggerts","content":"`decideAutoCompaction` returns an `AutoCompactionDecision` with a typed `reason`, the updated `state`, and diagnostics (`cooldownRemainingMs`, `tokenGrowth`, `tokensUntilRepeat`). Loop safeguards encoded in the code comments: unknown usage never triggers and never erases the baseline; in-flight compactions suppress triggers; every repeat honours cooldown; and if usage remains above threshold after compaction, the first known sample is only a baseline and a repeat requires `repeatMinGrowthTokens` of growth."},"2260":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-108","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#26-auto-compaction-trigger-auto-triggerts","content":"**Runtime wiring** (`src/index.ts&#x60;): the decision runs on &#x2A;*`agent_end`**, not `turn_end`. The code explains why: `ctx.compact()` aborts the active agent operation first, so compacting between turns of a still-running loop would kill the next in-flight provider request. `agent_end` fires only after the run has settled, matching Pi core's own native check point. On trigger, `ctx.compact({ customInstructions: COMPACTOR_INSTRUCTION, onComplete, onError })` is called; `onComplete` → `markAutoCompactionComplete`, `onError` → `markAutoCompactionError` (benign errors \"Compaction cancelled\"/\"Already compacted\" are not surfaced)."},"2261":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-109","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#27-configuration","content":"`src/config/manager.ts` loads a global config from `~/.unipi/config/compactor/config.json` (scaffolded from `DEFAULT_COMPACTOR_CONFIG` on first run) and deep-merges optional per-project overrides from `<cwd>/.unipi/config/compactor.json`. `migrateConfig` fills missing keys so older files keep working. `CompactorConfig` (`types.ts`) groups:"},"2262":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-110","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#27-configuration","content":"**Strategies** (`CompactorStrategyConfig` = `{ enabled, mode, autoDetect? }`): `sessionGoals`, `filesAndChanges`, `commits` (auto-disabled at runtime when `autoDetect: \"git\"` and no `.git` directory exists), `outstandingContext`, `userPreferences`, `briefTranscript`, `sessionContinuity`, `sandboxExecution`; `fts5Index` is retained only for compatibility."},"2263":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-111","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#27-configuration","content":"**Pipeline**: `autoInjection`, `customNoisePatterns`."},"2264":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-112","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#27-configuration","content":"**`autoCompaction`** (see §2.6)."},"2265":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-113","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#27-configuration","content":"**Global**: `overrideDefaultCompaction`, `smartKeepTail`, `continueAfterThresholdCompact`, `debug` (writes `/tmp/compactor-debug.json`)."},"2266":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-114","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#27-configuration","content":"`config/presets.ts` provides named presets (`precise`, `balanced`, `thorough`, `lean`, `opencode`, `verbose`, `minimal`, `custom`) and a settings TUI (`tui/settings-overlay.ts`) edits them interactively."},"2267":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-115","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"`SessionDB` is a SQLite store at `~/.unipi/db/compactor/session.db` (WAL mode). It prefers `bun:sqlite` and falls back to `better-sqlite3`, normalising the different constructor shapes. Initialization is fail-soft: `src/index.ts` only assigns `sessionDB` after `init()` succeeds, so a partially constructed instance never slips past null-guards and dependent commands report \"not initialized\" gracefully."},"2268":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-116","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"**Session identity.** `getWorktreeSuffix()` appends `__<sha256(cwd)[0:8]>` when the current directory is a non-main git worktree (or honours `COMPACTOR_SESSION_SUFFIX`), so parallel worktrees on the same Pi session id do not share state."},"2269":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-117","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"**Schema** (created idempotently, then migrated with `PRAGMA user_version`):"},"2270":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-118","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"Table"},"2271":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-119","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"Purpose"},"2272":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-120","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"Key columns"},"2273":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-121","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"`session_events`"},"2274":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-122","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"Append-only behavioural events extracted from tool results"},"2275":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-123","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"`type`, `category`, `priority`, `data`, `data_hash`, `attribution_source`, `attribution_confidence`, `source_hook`"},"2276":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-124","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"`session_meta`"},"2277":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-125","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"One row per session"},"2278":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-126","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"`event_count`, `compact_count`, `total_chars_before`, `total_chars_kept`, `total_messages_summarized`, `sandbox_runs`, `search_queries`"},"2279":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-127","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"`session_resume`"},"2280":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-128","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"One-shot resume snapshot per session"},"2281":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-129","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"`snapshot`, `event_count`, `consumed`"},"2282":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-130","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"Migrations V1 and V2 add columns with a `safeAddColumn` helper that tolerates \"duplicate column\" errors, because SQLite auto-commits DDL and a partially applied prior run must not break startup."},"2283":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-131","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#31-sessiondb-srcsessiondbts","content":"**Write discipline.** `insertEvent` runs in a transaction: it de-duplicates against the last `DEDUP_WINDOW = 5` events by `(type, data_hash)`, evicts the lowest-priority oldest event when a session exceeds `MAX_EVENTS_PER_SESSION = 1000`, and bumps `session_meta.event_count`. `cleanupOldSessions(7)` runs on `session_shutdown`."},"2284":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-132","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#32-event-capture-srcsessionextractts","content":"On every `tool_result`, `extractEventsFromToolResult` converts the tool call into zero or more `SessionEvent`s with priorities (`LOW`=1 … `CRITICAL`=4): `tool_error` (HIGH), `file_read`/`file_edit`/`file_write` (NORMAL), `bash_executed` (LOW), `git_operation` (NORMAL), `sandbox_execution` (LOW), `content_search` (LOW). The tool response is truncated to 1000 characters before extraction."},"2285":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-133","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#33-resume-snapshot-and-injection","content":"Two handlers cooperate around a compaction:"},"2286":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-134","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#33-resume-snapshot-and-injection","content":"`src/index.ts&#x60; on &#x2A;*`session_before_compact`** (when `sessionContinuity` is enabled) loads up to 1000 events and stats, builds an XML snapshot via `session/snapshot.ts#buildResumeSnapshot` — `<files>` (last 10 active files with op counts), `<errors>`, `<decisions>`, each with a suggested recall tool call — and `upsertResume`s it (resetting `consumed = 0`)."},"2287":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-135","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#33-resume-snapshot-and-injection","content":"On the next &#x2A;*`before_agent_start`**, `resume-inject.ts#buildResumeContextMessage` calls `injectResumeSnapshot`, which returns the snapshot once (then `markResumeConsumed`), optionally appending `buildAutoInjection(events)` when `pipeline.autoInjection` is on. The result is delivered as a **hidden custom message** (`customType: \"unipi-compactor-resume\"`, `display: false`) rather than a system-prompt change — the comment notes this preserves Pi's stable prompt prefix for provider cache reuse."},"2288":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-136","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#34-recall-session_recall-unipisession-recall","content":"`session/recall-blocks.ts#recallBlocksFromContext` reads the **append-only session branch** (`ctx.sessionManager.getBranch()`), not the compacted LLM context, so raw pre-compaction messages remain searchable. It normalizes standard roles via `normalizeMessages` and handles Pi-specific roles (`bashExecution`, `custom`, `branchSummary`, `compactionSummary`) plus `custom_message`, `branch_summary` and `compaction` entries, tagging each block with its `sourceIndex`. `src/index.ts` also caches filtered blocks on `before_agent_start` as a fallback."},"2289":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-137","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#34-recall-session_recall-unipisession-recall","content":"The `session_recall` tool (`tools/register.ts`, deprecated alias `vcc_recall`) accepts `query` (keywords, regex, or `#N:path` drill-down), `expand` (indices to return untruncated), `page`, `scope` (`lineage` | `all` to include edited/retried branches) and `mode` (`hybrid` | `touched` — files aggregated by path). It delegates to `tools/vcc-recall.ts`, which reuses `search-entries.ts`, `touched-files.ts` and `drill-down.ts`. The slash command variant sends results as a visible custom message *and* feeds them to the agent with `triggerTurn` so recall drives the next turn."},"2290":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-138","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"All tools are registered on `session_start` once `SessionDB` is live, via `registerCompactorTools(pi, deps)` with TypeBox schemas:"},"2291":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-139","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"Tool"},"2292":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-140","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"Purpose"},"2293":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-141","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"`compact`"},"2294":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-142","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"Manual compaction; `dryRun: true` previews counts without compacting"},"2295":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-143","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"`session_recall` (alias `vcc_recall`)"},"2296":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-144","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"Search session history (see §3.4)"},"2297":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-145","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"`sandbox` / `sandbox_file` / `sandbox_batch` (aliases `ctx_execute`, `ctx_execute_file`, `ctx_batch_execute`)"},"2298":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-146","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"Execute code in 11 languages inside the sandbox; only registered when `sandboxExecution` is enabled"},"2299":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-147","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"`compactor_stats` (alias `ctx_stats`)"},"2300":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-148","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"Session and all-time compaction statistics"},"2301":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-149","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"`compactor_doctor` (alias `ctx_doctor`)"},"2302":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-150","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"Diagnostics on the compactor installation"},"2303":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-151","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"`context_budget`"},"2304":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-152","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"Token-budget introspection built on `token-estimate.ts`"},"2305":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-153","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#41-registered-surface","content":"Slash commands (`commands/index.ts`) include `/unipi:lossless-compact` (alias `/unipi:compact`) which calls `ctx.compact({ customInstructions: COMPACTOR_INSTRUCTION })` and reports `getLastCompactionStats()` on completion, plus `/unipi:session-recall` and preset/settings commands. The module announces itself with `MODULE_READY` carrying `COMPACTOR_COMMANDS` and `COMPACTOR_TOOLS` from core, and registers a `compactor` info-screen group (tokens saved, cost saved, % reduction, top tools, compactions, tool calls) backed by `src/info-screen.ts`."},"2306":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-154","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#42-polyglotexecutor-srcexecutorexecutorts","content":"A sandboxed runner for `javascript`, `typescript`, `python`, `shell`, `ruby`, `go`, `rust`, `php`, `perl`, `r`, `elixir`. It detects available runtimes (`runtime.ts#detectRuntimes`), writes code to a temp directory, and enforces an output hard cap (`sandboxExecution.outputLimit`, default 100 MiB). Security measures:"},"2307":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-155","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#42-polyglotexecutor-srcexecutorexecutorts","content":"`sanitizeEnv()` removes an explicit `DANGEROUS_ENV_VARS` list (cloud credentials, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `NPM_TOKEN`, `DATABASE_URL`, …) and any variable whose name contains `SECRET`, `PASSWORD`, `TOKEN` or `PRIVATE_KEY`."},"2308":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-156","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#42-polyglotexecutor-srcexecutorexecutorts","content":"`killTree()` terminates the whole process group (`taskkill /F /T` on Windows, `process.kill(-pid, \"SIGKILL\")` on POSIX); backgrounded PIDs are tracked and cleaned on `session_shutdown`."},"2309":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-157","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#43-security-policy-layer-srcsecurity","content":"The `input` hook in `src/index.ts` applies an advisory, **fail-open** security pass: `readsOrCreatesPolicy(cwd)` loads deny patterns from `.pi/settings.json`; `evaluateCommand` blocks bash commands matching deny patterns (returning an error tool result); `hasShellEscapes`/`scanForShellEscapes` inspect non-shell sandbox code; `evaluateFilePath` checks read/edit/write paths. A hard-coded guard also cancels bash commands invoking `curl|wget|nc|netcat`. Errors in the security path never block execution — enforcement is intentionally left to the hooks system."},"2310":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-158","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#44-display-safety","content":"The `tool_result` hook clamps `details.diff` of `edit`/`write` results to the terminal width (`display/diff-width-safety.ts#clampDiffToWidth`) because Pi's diff renderer does not truncate lines and could crash the TUI on narrow terminals."},"2311":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-159","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#51-storage-model","content":"`packages/memory/storage.ts` defines the record shape and the `MemoryStorage` class:"},"2312":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-160","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#51-storage-model","content":"Storage is **project-scoped**: `getProjectName(cwd)` sanitizes the last path segment, and each project owns `~/.unipi/memory/<project>/`. Two tiers are maintained:"},"2313":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-161","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#51-storage-model","content":"**MemPalace** (primary, queryable) — a \"palace\" at `~/.mempalace/palace` with one \"wing\" per project."},"2314":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-162","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#51-storage-model","content":"**Markdown tier** (durable, human-readable) — `<id>.md` files with YAML frontmatter (`id`, `title`, `tags`, `project`, `created`, `updated`, `type`). `storeMempalace` writes the palace first and then the markdown copy best-effort, so the file tier stays a consistent fallback and migration source."},"2315":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-163","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#52-mempalace-bridge-mempalacets","content":"The TypeScript ↔ Python boundary is a **processless CLI protocol**: each operation spawns the MemPalace venv Python with `[bridgePath, palace, cmd, argsJson]` and parses a single JSON line `{ ok, result?, error? }`. `runBridge` is synchronous (`spawnSync`, 60 s default timeout, 64 MiB buffer); `runBridgeAsync` is the non-blocking twin used wherever the UI is live (status bar, info overlay), because a synchronous Python round-trip takes \\~0.5–1.1 s. Any failure — timeout, non-zero exit, malformed JSON, `ok: false` — yields `null`; callers treat `null` as \"no data\"."},"2316":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-164","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#52-mempalace-bridge-mempalacets","content":"Installation and health are cached with flag files under `~/.unipi/memory/`:"},"2317":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-165","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#52-mempalace-bridge-mempalacets","content":"`ensureMempalace()` locates the venv Python via `uv tool dir`, or installs with `uv tool install mempalace` (180 s timeout) when `uv` is present; the result is cached in `.mempalace-install`."},"2318":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-166","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#52-mempalace-bridge-mempalacets","content":"A `ping` sanity check is skipped when `.mempalace-ping-verified` is younger than 24 h; the flag is invalidated on any failed bridge call so a broken palace is re-verified next session."},"2319":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-167","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#52-mempalace-bridge-mempalacets","content":"`maybeAutoUpdateMempalace()` performs a TTL-gated (\\~daily) PyPI check and `uv tool upgrade`, emitting `UPDATE_APPLIED` on success."},"2320":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-168","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#52-mempalace-bridge-mempalacets","content":"`resolveMempalaceBridgePath` supports the standalone package layout, the umbrella bundle layout, an `UNIPI_MEMPALACE_BRIDGE` override, and `require.resolve(\"@pi-unipi/memory/package.json\")` for non-hoisted installs."},"2321":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-169","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#53-migration-with-verified-resumable-state","content":"Legacy data (markdown files and a `memory.db` SQLite file) is migrated one-way into the palace. Rather than a one-shot timestamp, `getMemorySourceFingerprint` hashes the relative path, size and mtime of every durable source file; `isMigrated(fingerprint)` compares against `.mempalace-migrated` (`MIGRATION_STATE_VERSION = 2`). `markMigrated` refuses to record completion unless `result.failed === 0 && result.verified === result.discovered`, so a failed or partial run retries on a later session. Because new or changed markdown changes the fingerprint, catch-up migration is automatic. The first migration may embed thousands of records and is given a 15-minute window."},"2322":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-170","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#53-migration-with-verified-resumable-state","content":"**Fail-soft behaviour.** `MemoryStorage.init()` throws when MemPalace cannot be made available; `index.ts` catches this, sets `projectStorage = null`, and the extension runs without memory (\"Memory must never hard-fail\"). Note that the header comment in `mempalace.ts` still mentions a legacy SQLite fallback path, whereas the current `storage.ts` implementation treats SQLite solely as a migration source."},"2323":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-171","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#54-lifecycle-and-agent-nudging-indexts","content":"Hook"},"2324":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-172","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#54-lifecycle-and-agent-nudging-indexts","content":"Behaviour"},"2325":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-173","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#54-lifecycle-and-agent-nudging-indexts","content":"`session_start`"},"2326":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-174","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#54-lifecycle-and-agent-nudging-indexts","content":"Create `MemoryStorage` for the project, `init()`; defer orphaned-markdown sync to first storage access (`ensureOrphanSync`) to keep startup fast; kick off the TTL-gated auto-update; emit `MODULE_READY`; register the `memory` info group; set a status string (`🧠 mem <project>p/<all>all`, or `⚡`/`📝` when embeddings/markdown-only) asynchronously."},"2327":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-175","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#54-lifecycle-and-agent-nudging-indexts","content":"`before_agent_start`"},"2328":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-176","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#54-lifecycle-and-agent-nudging-indexts","content":"Once per session, inject a hidden `unipi-memory-recall-reminder` message built by `buildMemoryRecallReminder` listing up to 20 memory titles and instructing the agent to call `memory_search` before work and `memory_store` after. Only tools currently active (`pi.getActiveTools()`) are mentioned, so workflow sandboxes are respected."},"2329":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-177","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#54-lifecycle-and-agent-nudging-indexts","content":"`agent_end`"},"2330":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-178","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#54-lifecycle-and-agent-nudging-indexts","content":"If recall happened but nothing was stored, send a hidden `unipi-memory-retro-reminder` for the next turn."},"2331":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-179","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#54-lifecycle-and-agent-nudging-indexts","content":"`session_compact`"},"2332":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-180","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#54-lifecycle-and-agent-nudging-indexts","content":"Reset `recallDone` so the reminder is re-injected after compaction."},"2333":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-181","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#54-lifecycle-and-agent-nudging-indexts","content":"`session_shutdown`"},"2334":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-182","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#54-lifecycle-and-agent-nudging-indexts","content":"Close storage."},"2335":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-183","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#54-lifecycle-and-agent-nudging-indexts","content":"`tools.ts#memory_store` guards against duplicates: an exact title match with identical content returns a `duplicate_detected` result asking the agent to read first; same title with new content updates the record (regenerating the embedding via `embedding.ts#generateEmbedding`). `findSimilarByTitle` provides fuzzy matching for near-duplicates. Cross-project search/list (`searchAllProjects`, `listAllProjectsCachedAsync`, `global_memory_list`, alias `global_memory_search`) iterate all project directories."},"2336":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-184","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#61-cross-cutting-tracer","content":"Although grouped in this domain, `trajectory` acts as a **cross-cutting observability layer**: the umbrella entry (`packages/unipi/index.ts`) calls `createUnipiTracer(pi)` and wraps every other module's `ExtensionAPI` with `tracer.scope(packageName)`. The proxy fingerprints hook inputs and outputs so context mutations can be attributed to individual packages:"},"2337":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-185","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#61-cross-cutting-tracer","content":"`mutationSurface(event)` selects the part of an event that can mutate context (`context` → messages, `before_provider_request` → payload, `before_agent_start` → systemPrompt, `input` → text/images, `tool_result` → content/details/isError/usage, …)."},"2338":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-186","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#61-cross-cutting-tracer","content":"`mutationEvidence(before, after)` compares SHA-256 fingerprints of canonicalized values and, when they differ, records `firstDifference` (path, kind, sampled before/after)."},"2339":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-187","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#61-cross-cutting-tracer","content":"`CONTEXT_API_ACTIONS` (`sendMessage`, `sendUserMessage`, `setActiveTools`, `setModel`, `setThinkingLevel`, `registerProvider`, `unregisterProvider`) are traced as context-affecting API calls."},"2340":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-188","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#62-telemetry-sidecar-and-prefix-integrity","content":"`src/capture.ts#registerTelemetryCapture` registers read-only hooks that append `TelemetryEvent`s (`hook`, `unipi-trace`, `prefix-integrity`, `system-prompt`, `request`, `response`, `first-token`, `message-end`, `tool-start`, `tool-end`) to `~/.unipi/trajectory/<sessionId>.jsonl` via `TelemetrySidecar`. Safety properties of the sidecar:"},"2341":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-189","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#62-telemetry-sidecar-and-prefix-integrity","content":"Directory mode `0o700`, file mode `0o600`."},"2342":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-190","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#62-telemetry-sidecar-and-prefix-integrity","content":"`redactTelemetry` masks keys matching `authorization|api[-_]?key|token|cookie|secret|password|credential` and values that look like bearer tokens, `sk-…`, `gh[pousr]_…`, or Google API keys; strings are truncated at 200 000 chars; events over 2 MB are dropped."},"2343":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-191","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#62-telemetry-sidecar-and-prefix-integrity","content":"Only a 5 MB tail is retained in memory and re-read, so the live inspector never scans the whole file; a `revision` counter allows cheap change detection."},"2344":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-192","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#62-telemetry-sidecar-and-prefix-integrity","content":"`PrefixIntegrityTracker` (`prefix-integrity.ts`) fingerprints each provider request's messages, system prompt, tools and envelope, and classifies successive requests as `first_request`, `identical_retry`, `prefix_extended`, `boundary` (marked on `session_compact` and `session_tree`) or `violation` — surfacing when something breaks the stable prefix that provider prompt caching depends on."},"2345":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-193","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#63-live-trajectory-ui","content":"The `/unipi:trajectory` command (`index.ts`) starts a `TrajectoryServer`, opens the browser, and serves a snapshot built by `projectTrajectory(branchEntries, sessionMeta, telemetry)`. Snapshots are cached by `(leafId, telemetryRevision)`; `stop`/`off`/`toggle` arguments manage the server, which is also stopped on `session_shutdown`."},"2346":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-194","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#7-end-to-end-flow-compaction-persistence-and-recall","content":"Downstream, `notify` and `footer` react to `COMPACTOR_COMPACTED`/`MODULE_READY` without importing the compactor, and the info screen reads the registered data providers."},"2347":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-195","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#8-persistence-inventory","content":"Artifact"},"2348":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-196","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#8-persistence-inventory","content":"Path"},"2349":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-197","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#8-persistence-inventory","content":"Owner"},"2350":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-198","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#8-persistence-inventory","content":"Format / Notes"},"2351":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-199","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#8-persistence-inventory","content":"Compactor global config"},"2352":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-200","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#8-persistence-inventory","content":"`~/.unipi/config/compactor/config.json`"},"2353":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-201","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#8-persistence-inventory","content":"compactor"},"2354":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-202","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#8-persistence-inventory","content":"JSON, scaffolded from defaults, deep-merged with project overrides"},"2355":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-203","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain#8-persistence-inventory","content":"Compactor project override"},"2356":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-memory-management-domain-204","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/context-and-