ation/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-131","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#23-event-contract-eventsts","content":"Updater"},"2756":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-132","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#23-event-contract-eventsts","content":"`UPDATE_CHECK`, `UPDATE_AVAILABLE`, `UPDATE_APPLIED`, `UPDATE_ERROR`"},"2757":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-133","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#23-event-contract-eventsts","content":"`UnipiUpdateCheckEvent`, `UnipiUpdateAvailableEvent`, `UnipiUpdateAppliedEvent`, `UnipiUpdateErrorEvent { error, phase: \"check\" \\| \"install\" }`"},"2758":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-134","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#23-event-contract-eventsts","content":"**How `MODULE_READY` drives discovery.** Every package emits `MODULE_READY` on `session_start` with its name, version and registered commands/tools (see `utility/src/index.ts` and `updater/src/index.ts` for canonical examples). Consumers such as `notify` and `footer` subscribe to this event and light up integrations only for modules that actually announced themselves. This is what allows packages to be removed or disabled without breaking peers — there are no compile-time imports between feature modules for this purpose."},"2759":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-135","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#23-event-contract-eventsts","content":"**Emission helper.** `utils.ts#emitEvent(pi, name, payload)` wraps `pi.events.emit` in a `try/catch` and returns a boolean, so a misbehaving listener can never crash an emitter."},"2760":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-136","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#24-sandbox-primitives-sandboxts","content":"The sandbox module encodes **tool access levels for workflow commands**. It is a pure data + predicate module with no host dependency."},"2761":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-137","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#24-sandbox-primitives-sandboxts","content":"`SandboxLevel = \"read_only\" | \"brainstorm\" | \"write_unipi\" | \"review\" | \"full\"`"},"2762":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-138","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#24-sandbox-primitives-sandboxts","content":"`BLOCKED_TOOLS` — tools removed at each level:"},"2763":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-139","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#24-sandbox-primitives-sandboxts","content":"`read_only` → `write`, `edit`, `bash`"},"2764":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-140","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#24-sandbox-primitives-sandboxts","content":"`brainstorm` → `edit`"},"2765":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-141","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#24-sandbox-primitives-sandboxts","content":"`write_unipi` → `bash`"},"2766":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-142","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#24-sandbox-primitives-sandboxts","content":"`review`, `full` → nothing"},"2767":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-143","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#24-sandbox-primitives-sandboxts","content":"`FALLBACK_TOOLS` — legacy explicit allow-lists used only when no active tool list is supplied."},"2768":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-144","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#24-sandbox-primitives-sandboxts","content":"`COMMAND_SANDBOX` — maps each `WORKFLOW_COMMANDS` entry to a level (e.g. `brainstorm → \"brainstorm\"`, `plan → \"write_unipi\"`, `work → \"full\"`, `review-work → \"review\"`, `consultant`/`research`/`debug`/`scan-issues` → `\"read_only\"`)."},"2769":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-145","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#24-sandbox-primitives-sandboxts","content":"Public API: `getSandboxLevel(cmd)`, `getBlockedToolsForLevel(level)`, `filterToolsForLevel(level, activeTools)`, `getToolsForCommand(cmd, activeTools?)`, `isToolAllowed(level, tool)`, `hasWriteAccess(cmd)`, `hasBashAccess(cmd)`."},"2770":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-146","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#24-sandbox-primitives-sandboxts","content":"An important design note in the file header: the workflow package **enforces blocked names at `tool_call` time rather than mutating Pi's tool schemas**, \"so provider tool schemas and ordering remain stable\". This keeps the provider-side prompt prefix cache intact (see §3.5) — the sandbox is a call-time gate, not a schema rewrite. `filterToolsForLevel` deliberately subtracts only violating tools, preserving safe extension tools such as `memory_search`, `ask_user` and web tools."},"2771":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-147","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#25-tui-helpers","content":"Three modules exist to make terminal rendering safe and consistent across the 9+ overlay implementations in the suite."},"2772":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-148","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#25-tui-helpers","content":"**`tui-width.ts` — width invariants.** pi-tui's differential renderer throws (and writes `~/.pi/agent/pi-crash.log`) when any rendered line is wider than the terminal. The module encodes the invariant `visibleWidth(line) <= width` as pure arithmetic:"},"2773":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-149","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#25-tui-helpers","content":"`normalizeWidth(w)` — guards against `0`, negative, `NaN` and fractional widths observed during resize races."},"2774":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-150","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#25-tui-helpers","content":"`MIN_BORDERED_WIDTH = 12`, `shouldRenderBorder(w)`, `boxInnerWidth(w)` (= width − 2), `adaptiveInnerWidth(w)` (drop borders on narrow terminals), `contentWidth(available, reserved)`."},"2775":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-151","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#25-tui-helpers","content":"`safeRepeat(char, n)` / `safeRepeatCount(n)` — `String.prototype.repeat` throws on negative counts; these never do."},"2776":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-152","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#25-tui-helpers","content":"`WidthKeyedCache` — a render cache keyed on width, because `requestRender()` does not call `invalidate()` and a cache that ignores width returns stale over-wide lines after the terminal narrows."},"2777":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-153","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#25-tui-helpers","content":"Shared `ansi` escape table and `TOGGLE_ON` / `TOGGLE_OFF` glyphs for settings overlays."},"2778":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-154","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#25-tui-helpers","content":"**`tui-overlay.ts` — box drawing and theming.** `OverlayTheme` wraps an optional Pi `Theme` and falls back to raw ANSI when none is set. It supplies `fg`, `bold`, `bg`, `frameLine(content, innerWidth)` (│ … │ padded and truncated), `ruleLine` (├───┤) and `borderLine(innerWidth, \"top\" | \"bottom\")`. `frameOverlay(body, width, options)` wraps pre-rendered lines in an **opaque** rounded frame — every row is padded to full inner width and tinted with a background so the transcript cannot bleed through the overlay (Pi's compositor only paints cells a component returns)."},"2779":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-155","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#25-tui-helpers","content":"**`spinner-line.ts` — self-animating widget.** `createSpinnerLine({ text, colorSpinner?, frames?, intervalMs?, padLeft? })` returns a factory for `ctx.ui.setWidget()`. The component owns a `setInterval` (default 80 ms, braille frames) and calls `tui.requestRender()` each tick, stopping on `dispose()`. Returning `undefined` from `text()` collapses the line without disposing. This pattern lets slow-refreshing data (1 s task polls) still show a live spinner."},"2780":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-156","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#26-shared-state-slots","content":"Core hosts two kinds of process-wide state, chosen deliberately for synchronous hot-path reads that an async event bus cannot serve well."},"2781":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-157","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#26-shared-state-slots","content":"**`fusion-status.ts` — `Symbol.for` slot.** The fusion package owns the active lead/sidekick pair; the footer owns the frame that displays it. Rather than importing each other, both use a `Symbol.for(\"unipi.fusion.status\")` key on `globalThis`:"},"2782":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-158","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#26-shared-state-slots","content":"The header comment states this follows \"the same pattern as background-tasks' shared registry\". `Symbol.for` (rather than a plain property) is used so the singleton survives duplicate `node_modules` copies of the package."},"2783":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-159","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#26-shared-state-slots","content":"**`global-types.ts` + `global.d.ts` — string-keyed registries.** The older variant declares `globalThis.__unipi_info_registry`, `__unipi_footer_registry`, `__unipi_kanboard_registry` and `__unipi_mcp_stats`, with minimal structural interfaces (`InfoRegistryLike`, `FooterRegistryLike`, `McpStatsLike`) so consumers avoid `as any`. The updater, for example, calls `globalThis.__unipi_info_registry?.registerGroup(...)` to add an \"Updater\" group to the info screen."},"2784":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-160","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#26-shared-state-slots","content":"**`model-cache.ts` — file-backed registry snapshot.** `writeModelCache(models)` / `readModelCache()` persist `{ updatedAt, models: [{ provider, id, name? }] }` to `~/.unipi/config/models-cache.json` (resolved at call time so `HOME` changes are honoured). The utility package writes this on `session_start` from `ctx.modelRegistry`, enabling TUI pickers in other packages to list models without a live registry handle. Both operations are best-effort and never throw."},"2785":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-161","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#27-bounded-output-bounded-outputts","content":"`boundModelOutput(text, { maxBytes?, artifactPrefix?, artifactDir? })` implements the suite's policy that **the agent's context window is the scarcest resource**:"},"2786":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-162","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#27-bounded-output-bounded-outputts","content":"If `originalBytes <= maxBytes` (default `DEFAULT_MODEL_OUTPUT_BYTES = 64 KiB`, floor 1 KiB), return unchanged."},"2787":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-163","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#27-bounded-output-bounded-outputts","content":"Otherwise, if the text is at most `MAX_RAW_ARTIFACT_BYTES = 16 MiB`, write the complete text to a **private artifact** under `~/.unipi/tool-results/` (directory created `0o700`, refused if it is a symlink or group/world-accessible; file written `0o600` with `flag: \"wx\"` and a random UUID name)."},"2788":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-164","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#27-bounded-output-bounded-outputts","content":"Build a marker block (`--- output bounded by UniPi ---`, artifact path or warning, sizes, and a hint to use the `read` tool with offset/limit)."},"2789":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-165","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#27-bounded-output-bounded-outputts","content":"Keep a **75 % head / 25 % tail** split of the remaining budget, insert an `… N bytes omitted …` line, and byte-slice to guarantee the result never exceeds `maxBytes`. Slicing is UTF-8 aware and strips trailing replacement characters."},"2790":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-166","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#27-bounded-output-bounded-outputts","content":"The returned `BoundedOutput { text, truncated, originalBytes, visibleBytes, artifactPath? }` is used by MCP tool proxies, helper result packages and other large-output producers. The utility cleanup job (§3.2) later reaps these artifacts (`tool-result-*`, `mcp-*`, `helper-*`) after the temp retention period."},"2791":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-167","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#28-shared-utilities-utilsts","content":"Small, defensive helpers used across the suite:"},"2792":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-168","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#28-shared-utilities-utilsts","content":"Filesystem: `sanitize`, `ensureDir`, `tryDelete`, `tryRead`, `safeMtimeMs`, `tryRemoveDir`, `resolvePath`, `fileExists`, `writeFile`, `readJson<T>`, `writeJson`."},"2793":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-169","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#28-shared-utilities-utilsts","content":"Misc: `randomId`, `now`, `parseArgs` (quote-aware tokeniser), `formatTokens` (1234 → `1.2k`, 1.5 M → `1.5M`), `isActiveSnapshot`."},"2794":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-170","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#28-shared-utilities-utilsts","content":"Package resolution: `getPackageVersion(dir)`, `findPackageRoot(startDir, packageName, maxSteps = 10)` (walks up, and also probes sibling `node_modules/<name>`), `getInstalledPackageVersion`."},"2795":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-171","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#28-shared-utilities-utilsts","content":"`getPiVersion()` — resolves the host version by `realpath`-ing `process.argv[1]` and walking up to `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent`'s `package.json`. It is cached per process and **never spawns a subprocess**; the comment records that the previous `execSync(\"pi --version\")` cost \\~350 ms per call."},"2796":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-172","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#28-shared-utilities-utilsts","content":"`initUnipiDirs(cwd)` — creates the standard `.unipi/**` project layout; intended to be called on `session_start`."},"2797":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-173","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#28-shared-utilities-utilsts","content":"`emitEvent` — safe emitter (see §2.3)."},"2798":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-174","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#28-shared-utilities-utilsts","content":"`withHerdrBlocked(pi, label, fn)` — emits `herdr:blocked { active: true, label }` before awaiting a blocking UI and `{ active: false }` after (including on throw), so an external \"herdr\" integration can show *blocked* rather than *working*."},"2799":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-175","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#28-shared-utilities-utilsts","content":"`compareVersions(a, b)` / `isNewerVersion(latest, current)` — semver-ish comparison (strips `v`, splits on `.`/`-`, first three numeric parts). The updater re-exports these from `version.ts` for backward compatibility."},"2800":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-176","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#3-utility-lifecycle--diagnostics-pi-unipiutility","content":"The utility package is itself a Pi extension (`packages/utility/src/index.ts`) that bundles cross-cutting operational concerns. It registers thirteen `/unipi:*` commands (`continue`, `reload`, `status`, `cleanup`, `env`, `doctor`, `badge-name`, `badge-gen`, `badge-toggle`, `badge-settings`, `util-settings`, `prefix-cache`, `skills-settings`) and three tools (`ctx_batch`, `ctx_env`, `set_session_name`)."},"2801":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-177","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#31-process-lifecycle-lifecycleprocessts","content":"`ProcessLifecycle` is a global singleton (`getLifecycle()`, `disposeLifecycle()`) with a small state machine `running → shutting_down → error` plus an `orphaned` branch."},"2802":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-178","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#31-process-lifecycle-lifecycleprocessts","content":"**Orphan detection.** Records `process.ppid` at construction and polls every 30 s (`unref`'d timer) with `process.kill(ppid, 0)`. If the parent has vanished, state becomes `orphaned` and `shutdown(\"orphaned\")` runs."},"2803":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-179","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#31-process-lifecycle-lifecycleprocessts","content":"**Signal handling.** Installs one-shot `SIGTERM` / `SIGINT` handlers that run shutdown and then `process.exit(0)`."},"2804":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-180","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#31-process-lifecycle-lifecycleprocessts","content":"**Cleanup registry.** `registerCleanup(fn)` returns an unregister closure; `shutdown(reason)` drains all callbacks best-effort (one failure does not stop the others). The extension registers analytics disable here, and calls `lifecycle.shutdown(\"session_shutdown\")` on the Pi `session_shutdown` hook."},"2805":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-181","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"`cleanupStale(options)` runs five category scanners and returns a `CleanupReport { timestamp, results[], totalRemoved, totalBytesFreed }`:"},"2806":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-182","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"Category"},"2807":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-183","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"Target"},"2808":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-184","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"Rule"},"2809":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-185","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"`db`"},"2810":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-186","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"`*.db`, `*.sqlite`, `*.sqlite3` under `~/.unipi/` (recursive)"},"2811":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-187","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"Older than `dbMaxAgeDays` (14) **or** has a WAL file older than 5 min (zombie lock); companions `-wal`, `-shm`, `-journal` removed too"},"2812":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-188","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"`temp`"},"2813":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-189","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"OS tmpdir entries matching `^unipi-`, `^pi-`, `\\.unipi\\.`"},"2814":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-190","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"Older than `tempMaxAgeDays` (7)"},"2815":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-191","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"`tool-results`"},"2816":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-192","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"`~/.unipi/tool-results/(tool-result\\|mcp-*\\|helper)-<uuid>.txt`"},"2817":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-193","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"Older than `tempMaxAgeDays` — reaps bounded-output artifacts"},"2818":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-194","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"`session`"},"2819":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-195","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"Directories under `~/.unipi/sessions`"},"2820":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-196","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"Older than `sessionMaxAgeDays` (30)"},"2821":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-197","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"`cache`"},"2822":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-198","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"Files under `~/.unipi/cache`"},"2823":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-199","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"Older than `tempMaxAgeDays`"},"2824":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-200","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#32-stale-cleanup-lifecyclecleanupts","content":"`dryRun: true` counts without deleting. `formatCleanupReport` renders markdown (first 10 paths per category). The `/unipi:cleanup` command wires this up and emits `UTILITY_CLEANUP_DONE`."},"2825":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-201","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#33-diagnostics-engine-diagnosticsenginets","content":"A plugin-based health checker. `registerDiagnosticPlugin(plugin)` appends to an in-memory plugin list; `runDiagnostics()` executes every plugin (isolating failures as `<plugin>_error` checks), aggregates counts, and derives `overall` as `error > warning > healthy > unknown`."},"2826":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-202","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#33-diagnostics-engine-diagnosticsenginets","content":"Built-in plugins (all attributed to `@pi-unipi/core`):"},"2827":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-203","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#33-diagnostics-engine-diagnosticsenginets","content":"`core_directories` — `~/.unipi` (required), `~/.unipi/memory`, `~/.unipi/cache`, `~/.unipi/analytics` (optional); checks existence and writability, with `mkdir -p` / `chmod u+w` suggestions."},"2828":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-204","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#33-diagnostics-engine-diagnosticsenginets","content":"`config_files` — validates `~/.unipi/config/mcp/servers.json` and `.unipi/config/mcp/servers.json` parse as JSON."},"2829":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-205","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#33-diagnostics-engine-diagnosticsenginets","content":"`node_environment` — Node ≥ 18 check and heap usage (> 512 MB → warning)."},"2830":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-206","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#33-diagnostics-engine-diagnosticsenginets","content":"`formatDiagnosticsReport` groups results errors-first in markdown. Exposed via `/unipi:doctor` with `UTILITY_DIAGNOSTICS_START/DONE` events."},"2831":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-207","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#34-analytics-collector-analyticscollectorts","content":"`AnalyticsCollector` (singleton via `getAnalyticsCollector()`) keeps an **in-memory** ring of `AnalyticsEvent { id, type, timestamp, metadata }` with types `module_load | command_run | tool_call | error | compaction | search`. Typed helpers: `recordCommand`, `recordTool`, `recordError`, `recordModuleLoad`, `recordSearch`. `getRollup(date?)` computes a per-day `AnalyticsRollup`. Metadata passes through `sanitizeMetadata`, which redacts sensitive keys; `flush()` runs every 60 s and on buffer-full but currently only trims to `maxEvents` (10 000) — the SQLite persistence is an explicit `TODO`. The `dbPath` default `~/.unipi/analytics/events.db` is reserved for that future."},"2832":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-208","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#35-provider-prefix-cache-observability-prefix-cachets","content":"`PrefixCacheTracker` answers the operational question \"is my provider prompt-prefix cache being invalidated?\" without ever retaining prompts."},"2833":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-209","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#35-provider-prefix-cache-observability-prefix-cachets","content":"Each request payload observed via the `before_provider_request` hook is **canonicalised** (sorted keys, cycle-safe, bigint/NaN/bytes tagged) and fingerprinted with an **HMAC-SHA256 under a random per-session 32-byte key** (first 16 hex chars kept). The key is never persisted, so fingerprints cannot be correlated across processes or used as a dictionary oracle."},"2834":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-210","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#35-provider-prefix-cache-observability-prefix-cachets","content":"The sequence field (`messages` | `input` | `contents`) is fingerprinted item-by-item; everything else plus the model route (`provider/id/api`) forms the *envelope*."},"2835":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-211","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#35-provider-prefix-cache-observability-prefix-cachets","content":"Transitions are classified as `first_request`, `prefix_extended`, `identical_retry`, `envelope_changed`, `payload_shape_changed` or `history_rewritten`; boundary transitions bump an `epoch` counter."},"2836":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-212","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#35-provider-prefix-cache-observability-prefix-cachets","content":"`observeMessages` (on `agent_end`) accumulates `input/output/cacheRead/cacheWrite` usage from assistant messages, deduplicating by object identity because `agent_end` re-exposes the whole context."},"2837":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-213","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#35-provider-prefix-cache-observability-prefix-cachets","content":"`markBoundary(...)` is invoked from `model_select`, `thinking_level_select`, `session_compact` and `session_tree` hooks so lifecycle-driven boundaries are attributed correctly before the next payload arrives."},"2838":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-214","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#35-provider-prefix-cache-observability-prefix-cachets","content":"`formatPrefixCacheStats` renders the snapshot for `/unipi:prefix-cache`, including observed cache-read share. The tracker is reset on `session_start`."},"2839":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-215","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#36-skill-discovery-gate-skill-discoveryts","content":"Controls the `unipi.skills.discovery` flag in Pi's `settings.json` (`$PI_AGENT_DIR` or `~/.pi/agent`). When disabled, the `before_agent_start` hook strips Unipi's bundled skills from the `<available_skills>…</available_skills> ` block of the system prompt every turn — user skills stay listed and `/skill:name` invocation is unaffected because Pi reads `SKILL.md` directly. Applying the filter consistently per turn keeps the provider prefix cache stable."},"2840":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-216","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#37-environment-tool-toolsenvts-and-info-screen-integration","content":"`getEnvironmentInfo()` collects Node version, `getPiVersion()`, OS/arch, installed `@pi-unipi/*` modules discovered from `node_modules/@pi-unipi`, config paths (`~/.unipi/config`, `.unipi/config`) and `~/.pi`. `formatEnvironmentInfo` renders a markdown table. This backs both the `ctx_env` tool and `/unipi:env`."},"2841":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-217","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#37-environment-tool-toolsenvts-and-info-screen-integration","content":"`info-screen.ts` emits `INFO_GROUP_REGISTERED` for a `utility` group and exposes `getUtilityStats()` (uptime, lifecycle state, orphan flag, today's event/error counts)."},"2842":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-218","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#38-extension-entry-behaviour-srcindexts","content":"On load the entry initialises lifecycle, analytics and the prefix tracker, registers commands and tools, and wires hooks. On `session_start` it emits `MODULE_READY` for `MODULES.UTILITY`, records a `module_load` analytics event, restores/shows the name badge, and **writes the model cache** from `ctx.modelRegistry`. A first-message/`agent_end` pair captures a ≤ 800-char conversation summary and emits `BADGE_GENERATE_REQUEST` so a background agent (in another package) can propose a session name. The `set_session_name` tool is registered only when `badgeSettings.agentTool` is enabled — an example of the suite's config-gated tool registration."},"2843":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-219","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#41-responsibilities-and-commands","content":"The updater keeps the umbrella package current and doubles as a documentation browser. It registers:"},"2844":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-220","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#41-responsibilities-and-commands","content":"`/unipi:readme [package]` — README browser over the root and per-package READMEs (`readme.ts` discovers them via `findPackageRoot(…, \"@pi-unipi/unipi\")` and `node_modules/@pi-unipi/<name>/README.md`)."},"2845":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-221","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#41-responsibilities-and-commands","content":"`/unipi:changelog` — Keep-a-Changelog browser."},"2846":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-222","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#41-responsibilities-and-commands","content":"`/unipi:updater-settings` — check interval and auto-update mode editor."},"2847":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-223","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#41-responsibilities-and-commands","content":"All three open `ctx.ui.custom(...)` overlays with `width: \"80%\"`, `minWidth: 60`, centered."},"2848":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-224","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#42-configuration-and-cache","content":"`settings.ts` — `UpdaterConfig { checkIntervalMs, autoUpdate: \"disabled\" | \"notify\" | \"auto\" }` stored at `~/.unipi/config/updater/config.json`. Defaults: 1 h interval, `notify`. Valid intervals: 30 min, 1 h, 6 h, 1 d. Load failures fall back to defaults silently."},"2849":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-225","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#42-configuration-and-cache","content":"`cache.ts` — `LastCheckCache { lastCheck, latestVersion, skippedVersion? }` at `~/.unipi/cache/updater/last-check.json`, with `isCheckDue(intervalMs)`, `writeSkippedVersion`, `isVersionSkipped`."},"2850":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-226","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#43-update-check-checkerts","content":"`checkForUpdates()` resolves the installed `@pi-unipi/unipi` version by walking up from the updater's own location, then:"},"2851":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-227","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#43-update-check-checkerts","content":"If a cache exists and the interval has not elapsed, return the cached answer — **unless** the cached npm version is older than the installed version (which happens right after a local/source release), in which case the interval is ignored and a fresh fetch is forced."},"2852":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-228","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#43-update-check-checkerts","content":"`fetch(\"https://registry.npmjs.org/@pi-unipi/unipi\")` with a 10 s `AbortSignal.timeout`, read `dist-tags.latest`, write the cache."},"2853":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-229","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#43-update-check-checkerts","content":"`toUpdateResult` uses `isNewerVersion`, so a stale or downgraded registry state is never reported as an update."},"2854":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-230","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#43-update-check-checkerts","content":"On network error, return cached info (still guarded against downgrades) plus an `error` string."},"2855":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-231","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#44-session-start-flow-srcindexts","content":"Any failure in the check path is swallowed (\"silent, non-critical\"), consistent with the suite's fail-soft principle."},"2856":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-232","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#45-changelog-handling","content":"`changelog.ts` — `resolveChangelogPath()` locates the shipped `CHANGELOG.md` from the module's own location (not `process.cwd()`, which only worked inside a repo checkout), falling back to the working directory. `parseChangelogContent` parses `## [x.y.z] — YYYY-MM-DD` / `## [Unreleased]` headers and `### Section` blocks into `ChangelogEntry { version, date, sections, body }`. `getNewerVersions(entries, current)` filters by `isNewerVersion`."},"2857":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-233","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#45-changelog-handling","content":"`remote-changelog.ts` — `fetchRemoteChangelog(version)` fetches `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Neuron-Mr-White/unipi/v<version>/CHANGELOG.md` (5 s timeout), falling back to `main` on 404. Only the immutable tag response is cached (`~/.unipi/cache/updater/changelog-<version>.md`); the `main` fallback is never cached. `loadUpdateChangelog` prefers remote entries newer than the current version, falling back to the local changelog."},"2858":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-234","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#46-installer-and-overlay","content":"`installer.ts` — `installUpdate()` runs `pi install npm:@pi-unipi/unipi` via promisified `child_process.exec` with a 60 s timeout, then re-reads the installed version. Errors surface `stderr` when present."},"2859":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-235","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#46-installer-and-overlay","content":"`tui/update-overlay.ts` — renders the version diff and wrapped changelog entries (using `boxInnerWidth` from core and `renderMarkdown`), supports scrolling, `[Y] Update / [n] Skip`, and in `auto` mode a 5-second countdown that triggers `installUpdate()` unless cancelled. Skipping records the version so the prompt does not reappear for it."},"2860":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-236","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#51-composition-root-packagesunipiindexts","content":"The umbrella is a single default-exported `ExtensionAPI` function — \"the oh-my-zsh for pi\". It creates a trajectory tracer and loads every module through `tracer.scope(name)`, which returns a proxied `ExtensionAPI` that fingerprints hook inputs/outputs so context mutations can be attributed per package."},"2861":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-237","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#51-composition-root-packagesunipiindexts","content":"Verified load order:"},"2862":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-238","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#51-composition-root-packagesunipiindexts","content":"Two facts about this list are architecturally significant:"},"2863":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-239","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#51-composition-root-packagesunipiindexts","content":"**Order is load-bearing.** The inline comment explains that `utility` must precede `info-screen`: the name-badge overlay must sit at the *bottom* of the overlay stack because `hideOverlay()` pops the top entry and a capturing overlay's `done()` is one-shot; stacking the badge above the boot info-screen would strand the dashboard uncloseable. Nothing enforces this beyond the comment."},"2864":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-240","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#51-composition-root-packagesunipiindexts","content":"**Trajectory is cross-cutting.** It is loaded last with the plain (unscoped) `pi` and the shared recorder, so it observes every other module rather than being a peer feature."},"2865":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-241","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#52-bundling-scriptsbuild-bundlemjs","content":"Pi runs extensions through jiti with `moduleCache: false`, so transpiling \\~577 `.ts` files costs \\~1 s per startup. The build script produces `packages/unipi/bundled.js` (ESM, `platform: node`, `target: node22`) and cuts that to \\~80 ms. Two safeguards shape the output:"},"2866":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-242","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#52-bundling-scriptsbuild-bundlemjs","content":"**Externalise everything that is not ours.** An esbuild `onResolve` plugin bundles only relative imports and `@pi-unipi/*`; all third-party packages remain external and resolve from `node_modules` at runtime. The comment records that an earlier attempt inlined `node_modules` wholesale, which is why the bundle was gitignored as potentially carrying vendored credentials."},"2867":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-243","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#52-bundling-scriptsbuild-bundlemjs","content":"**Secret scan.** After emitting, the script greps the bundle for `sk-…`, `ghp_…`, `AKIA…`, `Bearer …` and `apiKey/secret/password = \"…\"` patterns and refuses to ship on a match."},"2868":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-244","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#52-bundling-scriptsbuild-bundlemjs","content":"`--if-missing` (used by the `prepare` hook) builds only when the bundle is absent and never fails an install if esbuild is unavailable — published tarballs already contain the bundle and no devDependencies."},"2869":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-245","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#53-root-manifest-and-version-pinning","content":"The root `package.json` (`@pi-unipi/unipi` 2.18.1) declares npm workspaces (`packages/*`), points `pi.extensions` at `packages/unipi/bundled.js`, enumerates per-package `skills/` directories under `pi.skills`, exposes `packages/subagents/prompts` as `pi.prompts`, and pins every `@pi-unipi/*` dependency to an exact version. Scripts: `build`, `prepare` (`--if-missing`), `prepublishOnly`, `publish:all` (`npm publish --workspaces`), `test`, `typecheck`."},"2870":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-246","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#53-root-manifest-and-version-pinning","content":"`scripts/sync-pins.mjs <x.y.z>` rewrites every `@pi-unipi/*` entry in `dependencies` and `peerDependencies` across the root and all `packages/*/package.json` files to the given version — the mechanism the release chore uses to keep exact pins consistent."},"2871":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-247","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#53-root-manifest-and-version-pinning","content":"> **Drift note.** The root `files` array references `docs/prefix-cache-architecture.md`, but the `docs/` directory is empty in the repository."},"2872":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-248","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#62-integration-channels-provided-by-this-domain","content":"Channel"},"2873":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-249","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#62-integration-channels-provided-by-this-domain","content":"Mechanism"},"2874":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-250","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain#62-integration-channels-provided-by-this-domain","content":"Typical use"},"2875":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/platform-core-and-shared-infrastructure-domain-251","page_id":"/docs/