le is that **markdown files on disk are the single source of truth**. The workflow package causes the LLM to write them, the milestone package reads and patches them, and the kanboard package projects them into a browser. No package in the domain maintains a database; the only cross-package coupling is the *file format*, not code."},"2989":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-52","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#11-position-in-the-unipi-architecture","content":"All three packages declare `@pi-unipi/core` as their **only** internal dependency. The composition root (`packages/unipi/index.ts`) loads `workflow` first in its fixed sequence and `milestone` → `kanboard` later, but none of the three relies on that ordering."},"2990":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-53","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#2-shared-kernel-contracts-used-by-the-domain","content":"Before examining each package, it is useful to know which `@pi-unipi/core` primitives the domain consumes. They define the vocabulary the three packages share."},"2991":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-54","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#21-constants-packagescoreconstantsts","content":"Constant"},"2992":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-55","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#21-constants-packagescoreconstantsts","content":"Value / purpose"},"2993":{"id":"/docs