shot mechanisms described below."},"3037":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-100","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#33-command-registration-and-dispatch-commandsts","content":"The command table is a static array of `WorkflowCommand` records:"},"3038":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-101","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#33-command-registration-and-dispatch-commandsts","content":"`registerWorkflowCommands(pi, options)` iterates the table and calls `pi.registerCommand(\"unipi:<name>\", { description, getArgumentCompletions, handler })`. The `options` object is the seam between `commands.ts` and `index.ts`:"},"3039":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-102","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#33-command-registration-and-dispatch-commandsts","content":"**Handler algorithm** (identical for all twenty commands):"},"3040":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-103","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#33-command-registration-and-dispatch-commandsts","content":"Build a `UnipiWorkflowEvent` `{ command, fullCommand: \"/unipi:<name>\", args }`."},"3041":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-104","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#33-command-registration-and-dispatch-commandsts","content":"Call `options.activateSandbox(event)`. If it returns `false&#x60; another workflow is already active; the handler notifies &#x2A;\"Another UniPi workflow is still active\"* and returns."},"3042":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-105","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#33-command-registration-and-dispatch-commandsts","content":"Read `skills/<skillName>/SKILL.md` relative to `import.meta.url`. A missing file is tolerated — the workflow proceeds without skill content."},"3043":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-106","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#33-command-registration-and-dispatch-commandsts","content":"Compose the user message:"},"3044":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-107","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#33-command-registration-and-dispatch-commandsts","content":"`pi.sendUserMessage(message, { deliverAs: \"followUp\" })`. If this throws synchronously, `options.abortWorkflow()` is called so no phantom lifecycle or sandbox is left behind, and the error is re-thrown."},"3045":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-108","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#33-command-registration-and-dispatch-commandsts","content":"Update the TUI: `ctx.ui.notify(\"Running /unipi:<name>\")` and `ctx.ui.setStatus(\"unipi-workflow\", \"⚡ wf:<name> ✓ rl|○ rl\")`."},"3046":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-109","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#33-command-registration-and-dispatch-commandsts","content":"The skill files themselves are the \"programme\" the LLM executes. For example, `skills/plan/SKILL.md` declares its own boundaries (\"MAY read specs… MAY NOT edit code\"), the command format `/unipi:plan specs:<path> <string(greedy)>`, the sandbox (`write` only to `.unipi/docs/`) and the output path `.unipi/docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>-plan.md`. This is how the workflow package produces the artefacts that the kanboard parsers later expect."},"3047":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-110","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#33-command-registration-and-dispatch-commandsts","content":"**Ralph bridge.** A twenty-first command, `/unipi:ralph-start&#x60;, is always registered. If ralph is not detected it warns &#x2A;\"Ralph module not detected. Install @unipi/ralph first.\"*; otherwise it sends `Start a ralph loop with this task: …` as a follow-up user message, delegating to ralph's own tooling."},"3048":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-111","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`getArgumentCompletions(prefix)` returns `CompletionItem[]` (`{ value, label, description }`) or `null` for free-text commands. Completions are derived from disk, not from an index:"},"3049":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-112","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"Command"},"3050":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-113","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"Source"},"3051":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-114","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`value` format"},"3052":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-115","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`plan`"},"3053":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-116","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`.unipi/docs/specs/*.md`"},"3054":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-117","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`specs:<file>`"},"3055":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-118","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`work`, `review-work`, `auto`"},"3056":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-119","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`.unipi/docs/plans/*.md`"},"3057":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-120","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`plan:<file>`"},"3058":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-121","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`fix`"},"3059":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-122","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`.unipi/docs/debug/*.md`"},"3060":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-123","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`debug:<file>`"},"3061":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-124","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`chore-execute`"},"3062":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-125","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`.unipi/docs/chore/*.md`"},"3063":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-126","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`chore:<file>`"},"3064":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-127","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`worktree-merge`, `worktree-create`"},"3065":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-128","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`git worktree list --porcelain`"},"3066":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-129","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"branch basename"},"3067":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-130","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#34-filesystem-backed-tab-completion","content":"`suggestFilesFrom(subdir, valuePrefix, descLabel, prefix)` lists `.md` files sorted by mtime (newest first) and filters by the last whitespace-separated token of the prefix. `suggestWorktrees()` shells out via `execFileSync` once per `cwd` and caches the result in a module-level `worktreeSuggestionsCache`. A defensive filter drops any item whose `value` is not a string before returning."},"3068":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-131","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#35-workflowlifecycle-lifecyclets","content":"This is a **single-slot state machine**: at most one workflow can be active per session. `complete(messages)` locates the last `assistant` message and treats the workflow as successful unless its `stopReason` is `\"error\"` or `\"aborted\"`. The injectable `now` clock exists for deterministic tests (`lifecycle.test.ts`)."},"3069":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-132","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"The entry point wires three concerns around a single mutable `sandboxCommand: string | null`."},"3070":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-133","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"**(a) Enforcement — `tool_call` hook.**"},"3071":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-134","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"Because this is a call-time veto rather than a change to the registered tool set, the provider sees an unchanged tool schema across turns — an intentional choice to preserve prompt-prefix caching."},"3072":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-135","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"**(b) Snapshot persistence — `before_agent_start` hook.**"},"3073":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-136","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"The sandbox state is made visible to the LLM through a **hidden, append-only custom message** of type `WORKFLOW_SANDBOX_SNAPSHOT_TYPE = \"unipi-workflow-sandbox-snapshot\"` rather than by editing the system prompt. Two lookups feed the decision:"},"3074":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-137","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"`latestEffectiveSandboxSnapshot(branch)` — scans `buildSessionContext(branch).messages` backwards for a `role: \"custom\"` message of that type (i.e. what the model currently sees)."},"3075":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-138","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"`latestHistoricalSandboxSnapshot(branch)` — scans raw `SessionEntry[]` for a `custom_message` entry of that type (state that compaction may have folded into summary prose)."},"3076":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-139","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"Decision logic:"},"3077":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-140","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"Condition"},"3078":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-141","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"Action"},"3079":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-142","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"Sandbox active and latest snapshot content equals `formatActiveSandboxSnapshot(command, level)`"},"3080":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-143","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"no-op"},"3081":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-144","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"Sandbox active otherwise"},"3082":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-145","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"append active snapshot (`display: false`, `details: {active: true, command, level}`)"},"3083":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-146","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"Sandbox inactive, prior snapshot exists and `isActiveSnapshot(prior)`"},"3084":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-147","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"append inactive snapshot (`details: {active: false}`)"},"3085":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-148","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"Sandbox inactive, no prior or prior already inactive"},"3086":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-149","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"no-op (clean sessions get no marker)"},"3087":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-150","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"`formatActiveSandboxSnapshot` emits a Markdown block headed `# UniPi Workflow Sandbox Snapshot` that states it *supersedes all prior snapshots*, lists the workflow, level, blocked tool names and the per-level prose from `sandboxRestrictions(level)`:"},"3088":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-151","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"`brainstorm` → write restricted to `.unipi/docs/specs/`, bash only for setup like `git init`/`mkdir`."},"3089":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-152","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"`write_unipi` → write restricted to `.unipi/docs/`, bash blocked."},"3090":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-153","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"all levels → do not attempt blocked tools; explain to the user if they request one."},"3091":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-154","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"**(c) Completion — `agent_end` hook.** `workflowLifecycle.complete(event.messages)` returns a `CompletedWorkflowEvent`; if present, `sandboxCommand` is cleared and `WORKFLOW_END` is emitted. The comment notes that `agent_end` is retained as the completion boundary for Pi 0.80.2 compatibility."},"3092":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-155","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#36-sandbox-enforcement-and-snapshot-persistence-indexts","content":"**(d) Discovery.** On `session_start` the module calls `initUnipiDirs()`, emits `MODULE_READY` `{ name: MODULES.WORKFLOW, version, commands: Object.values(WORKFLOW_COMMANDS), tools: [] }`, probes `pi.getAllTools()` for a tool named `ralph_start`, and sets the status line `⚡ wf ✓ rl` / `⚡ wf ○ rl`. It also subscribes to `MODULE_READY` and flips `ralphDetected` when `MODULES.RALPH` announces itself, so load order is irrelevant. `session_shutdown` resets all three pieces of state."},"3093":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-156","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#42-document-model-typests-and-file-format","content":"The canonical `MILESTONES.md` shape that `parseMilestones` understands:"},"3094":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-157","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#42-document-model-typests-and-file-format","content":"Parsing rules in `milestone.ts`:"},"3095":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-158","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#42-document-model-typests-and-file-format","content":"Frontmatter is recognised only if line 1 is `---`; `title` (quotes stripped), `created` and `updated` are captured."},"3096":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-159","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#42-document-model-typests-and-file-format","content":"`## <text>` opens a new phase; `> text` lines are concatenated into `phase.description`."},"3097":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-160","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#42-document-model-typests-and-file-format","content":"`- [ ] text` / `- [x] text` (case-insensitive `x`) become items with their 1-indexed `lineNumber`."},"3098":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-161","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#42-document-model-typests-and-file-format","content":"Missing files and unparseable lines never throw: `emptyDoc(filePath)` supplies a default document dated today."},"3099":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-162","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#42-document-model-typests-and-file-format","content":"`updateItemStatus(filePath, phaseName, itemText, checked)` matches by lower-cased, trimmed phase and item text, rewrites the checkbox mark, bumps the `updated:` frontmatter to today, and performs an **atomic write** (`<file>.tmp` + `renameSync`). It returns `false` when the file is missing or the item is not found — callers rely on this to skip unmatched items silently."},"3100":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-163","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#42-document-model-typests-and-file-format","content":"`getProgressSummary(filePath)` aggregates counts per phase, computes `percentComplete` (rounded) and selects `currentPhase` as the first phase with `done < total`, defaulting to the first phase name or `\"None\"`."},"3101":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-164","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#43-commands-commandsts","content":"Both commands follow the workflow package's pattern exactly — load `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, wrap it in `<skill_content>` tags and deliver it as a `followUp` user message:"},"3102":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-165","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#43-commands-commandsts","content":"Command"},"3103":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-166","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#43-commands-commandsts","content":"Description"},"3104":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-167","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#43-commands-commandsts","content":"Extras"},"3105":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-168","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#43-commands-commandsts","content":"`/unipi:milestone-onboard`"},"3106":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-169","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#43-commands-commandsts","content":"\"Create MILESTONES.md from existing workflow docs — scan, propose, refine, write\""},"3107":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-170","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#43-commands-commandsts","content":"—"},"3108":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-171","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#43-commands-commandsts","content":"`/unipi:milestone-update`"},"3109":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-172","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#43-commands-commandsts","content":"\"Sync MILESTONES.md with completed work — scan docs, diff checkboxes, auto-update\""},"3110":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-173","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#43-commands-commandsts","content":"`getArgumentCompletions` returns `all` plus every phase name from the current `MILESTONES.md`, each described as `<done>/<total> done`."},"3111":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-174","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#43-commands-commandsts","content":"The `milestone-update` skill instructs the model to scan `.unipi/docs/{specs,plans,quick-work}/` for files newer than the `updated` frontmatter date, diff checkbox states, auto-apply exact matches and ask the user about unmatched completions. Note that these commands do **not** activate a workflow sandbox — they are lightweight instruction dispatchers only."},"3112":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-175","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#44-lifecycle-hooks-hooksts","content":"**Progress snapshot before each agent turn.** `registerSessionStartHook(pi)` (despite its name) installs a `before_agent_start` handler that mirrors the workflow sandbox mechanism with its own custom type `MILESTONE_SNAPSHOT_TYPE = \"unipi-milestone-snapshot\"`:"},"3113":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-176","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#44-lifecycle-hooks-hooksts","content":"`formatMilestoneContext(path)` builds a `## Project Milestones` block with overall progress, per-phase counts and `Current focus: <phase>`; it returns `null` when there are no items."},"3114":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-177","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#44-lifecycle-hooks-hooksts","content":"`latestEffectiveSnapshot` / `latestHistoricalSnapshot` look up the model-visible and raw-history snapshot respectively."},"3115":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-178","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#44-lifecycle-hooks-hooksts","content":"If there is no context and no prior snapshot → no-op. If there is no context and the prior snapshot is already inactive → no-op. Otherwise `formatMilestoneSnapshot(workspace, context)` is compared with the latest content and appended only when it changed (`display: false`, `details: { active: context !== null, workspace }`)."},"3116":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-179","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#44-lifecycle-hooks-hooksts","content":"This keeps the model informed of milestone status without touching the system prompt and without emitting redundant messages every turn."},"3117":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-180","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#44-lifecycle-hooks-hooksts","content":"**Auto-sync at workflow end.** `registerSessionEndHook(pi)`:"},"3118":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-181","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#44-lifecycle-hooks-hooksts","content":"On `session_start` records `sessionStartMs`, captures `ctx.cwd` (because `process.cwd()` may change before shutdown), and snapshots the content of every file in `.unipi/docs/{specs,plans,quick-work}` into a `baselineSnapshots` map."},"3119":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-182","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#44-lifecycle-hooks-hooksts","content":"`syncModifiedDocs()&#x60; runs on &#x2A;*`UNIPI_EVENTS.WORKFLOW_END`*&#x2A; (emitted by the workflow package when its follow-up agent loop drains) and again on &#x2A;*`session_shutdown`** as a fallback. It skips entirely if `MILESTONES.md` does not exist, otherwise:"},"3120":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-183","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#44-lifecycle-hooks-hooksts","content":"`scanModifiedDocs(dirs, since)` lists files whose `safeMtimeMs` exceeds `sessionStartMs`."},"3121":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-184","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#44-lifecycle-hooks-hooksts","content":"`extractNewCompletions(file, baseline)` walks the current file tracking `##` phases; an item counts as newly completed if it is `[x]` now and either the same line was `[ ]` in the baseline, or the baseline contained an unchecked line with identical text."},"3122":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-185","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#44-lifecycle-hooks-hooksts","content":"For each `{ text, phase }` it calls `updateItemStatus(milestonesPath, phase, text, true)`; non-matching items (e.g. spec checklists with \"— covered in Task N\" suffixes) are silently ignored."},"3123":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-186","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#45-entry-point-indexts","content":"`milestoneExtension(pi)` registers both hooks and both commands, then registers an **info-screen group** if `globalThis.__unipi_info_registry` is present:"},"3124":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-187","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#45-entry-point-indexts","content":"Finally it emits `MODULE_READY` with `name: MODULES.MILESTONE`, `commands: [\"milestone-onboard\", \"milestone-update\"]` and a hard-coded `version: \"0.1.0\"` (unlike workflow, which reads the version from `package.json`)."},"3125":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-188","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#52-shared-vocabulary-typests","content":"`ParsedDoc` is the contract between the parser, server and UI layers. Every parser is required to be non-throwing: read failures become entries in `warnings` and an empty document is returned."},"3126":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-189","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"**`ParserRegistry` (`parser/index.ts`).** Holds an ordered `DocParser[]`. `parse(filePath)` returns the result of the *first* parser whose `canParse` matches, or `null`. `parseAll(dir)` calls the private `findDocFiles(dir)`, which walks the tree recursively, skips dot-directories and collects `*.md` files, then parses each. `createDefaultRegistry()` is async because it lazily `import()`s the parser modules, registering in order: six `CheckboxParser` instances, then `PlanParser`, then `MilestoneParser`. Since `MILESTONES.md` lives directly under `.unipi/docs/`, none of the path-regex parsers claim it before `MilestoneParser`."},"3127":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-190","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"**`parseFrontmatter(content)` (`parser/frontmatter.ts`).** If line 0 is `---`, collects `key: value` pairs (keys matching `\\w[\\w-]*`) until the closing `---` and returns `{ metadata, bodyStart }`. Without a closing fence it returns `bodyStart: 0` so the whole file is treated as body."},"3128":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-191","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"**`CheckboxParser` (`parser/checkbox-parser.ts`).** A config-driven class that, per its header comment, replaces seven previously separate parser classes. Each `CheckboxDocConfig` supplies:"},"3129":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-192","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"Field"},"3130":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-193","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"Meaning"},"3131":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-194","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"`type`"},"3132":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-195","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"`DocType` label"},"3133":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-196","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"`pathRegex`"},"3134":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-197","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"directory test, e.g. `/\\/specs\\//`"},"3135":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-198","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"`command`"},"3136":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-199","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"string or `(fileName) => string`; becomes `ParsedItem.command` (the copy-to-clipboard action)"},"3137":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-200","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-