,"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"`/unipi:chore-execute chore:<file>`"},"3165":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-228","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"title from `title` or `name`"},"3166":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-229","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"`review`"},"3167":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-230","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"`/reviews/`"},"3168":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-231","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"`/unipi:review-work`"},"3169":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-232","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"—"},"3170":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-233","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"Checkbox lines match `^\\s*-\\s*\\[([ xX])\\]\\s*(.*)$`; empty text is dropped; `[x]` → `done`, otherwise `todo`."},"3171":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-234","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"**`PlanParser` (`parser/plans.ts`).** Plans use a task-header/status-line format rather than checkboxes:"},"3172":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-235","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"`TASK_HEADER_PATTERN` accepts em-dash, en-dash or hyphen separators. When a status line follows a header, an item is emitted with `lineNumber` pointing at the header and `command: /unipi:work plan:<file>`. `STATUS_MAP` collapses the seven plan states (plus `reviewed`) into the four `ItemStatus` values: `unstarted`/`failed` → `todo`; `in-progress`/`awaiting_user`/`blocked` → `in-progress`; `completed`/`skipped` → `done`; `reviewed` → `reviewed`."},"3173":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-236","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"**`MilestoneParser` (`parser/milestones.ts`).** Matches `/MILESTONES\\.md$/i` and parses frontmatter title, `##` phases and checkboxes **inline**. The body comment is explicit: this \"avoids requiring `@pi-unipi/milestone` as a runtime dependency\". Items are prefixed with the phase name — `[Phase 1: Foundation] Authentication system` — so the UI can regroup them, and each carries `command: /unipi:milestone-update`. Empty checkbox text produces a `Line N: Empty checkbox text` warning."},"3174":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-237","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#53-parser-layer","content":"> **Documentation drift:** the file header still says it \"imports `parseMilestones` from `@pi-unipi/milestone`\"; the implementation does not, and `kanboard/package.json` lists only `@pi-unipi/core`. The two parsers are format-compatible but maintained separately."},"3175":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-238","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#54-http-server-serverindexts","content":"`KanboardServer` is a thin wrapper over `node:http` with no framework dependency."},"3176":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-239","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#54-http-server-serverindexts","content":"Method"},"3177":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-240","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#54-http-server-serverindexts","content":"Behaviour"},"3178":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-241","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#54-http-server-serverindexts","content":"`constructor(config?)`"},"3179":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-242","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#54-http-server-serverindexts","content":"Defaults: `port 8165`, `maxPort 8175`, `docsRoot \".unipi/docs\"`, `pidFile \".unipi/kanboard.pid\"`. Resolves `staticDir` to `../ui/static` relative to the module."},"3180":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-243","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#54-http-server-serverindexts","content":"`route(method, pattern, handler)`"},"3181":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-244","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#54-http-server-serverindexts","content":"Converts Express-style `:param` segments into `([^/]+)` capture groups and stores `{ method, pattern: RegExp, paramNames, handler }`."},"3182":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-245","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#54-http-server-serverindexts","content":"`start()`"},"3183":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-246","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain#54-http-server-serverindexts","content":"Creates the server, calls `allocatePort()` (walks `port..maxPort`, skipping `EADDRINUSE`), writes the PID file, installs `SIGINT`/`SIGTERM` handlers that close the server, remove the PID file and `process.exit(0)`, and returns `{ port, url }`."},"3184":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain-247","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/structured-development-workflow-doma