d-presentation-domain-54","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#103-keyboard-shortcuts","content":"10.3 Keyboard shortcuts"},"3423":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-55","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#104-key-source-files","content":"10.4 Key source files"},"3424":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-56","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","content":"**Project:** Unipi (`@pi-unipi/*` extension suite for the Pi coding agent)\n&#x2A;*Domain type:** Presentation / Interaction\n&#x2A;*Packages:** `footer`, `ask-user`, `input-shortcuts`, `notify`, `info-screen`, `autocomplete` (published as `@pi-unipi/command-enchantment`), `btw`\n&#x2A;*Document date:** 2026-09-16"},"3425":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-57","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#1-domain-overview","content":"The User Interaction & Presentation domain owns every surface the developer sees or touches in the terminal beyond the raw chat stream. It is a purely *consuming* domain: it reads state produced by the orchestration, context, integration and workflow domains, renders that state into the TUI, and feeds user intent back into the system through tool results, slash commands, and events. No business rules about agents, compaction, or MCP servers live here — only the rules about how to present them and how to collect input."},"3426":{"id":"/docs/deep-explorati