/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#27-lifecycle-and-ui-slots","content":"Background-process one-liner (`renderProcessLine`)"},"3533":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-165","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#27-lifecycle-and-ui-slots","content":"`setWidget(\"footer-secondary\")`"},"3534":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-166","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#27-lifecycle-and-ui-slots","content":"`belowEditor`"},"3535":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-167","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#27-lifecycle-and-ui-slots","content":"—"},"3536":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-168","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#27-lifecycle-and-ui-slots","content":"Centered session strip: `n turn · n steps \\| wall · tool \\| avg ttft · tok/s \\| cache %`"},"3537":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-169","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#27-lifecycle-and-ui-slots","content":"The 1 s timer re-scans the session branch to reconcile TPS records after compactions, branch switches or reloads, computes branch-derived tool wall time by pairing `toolCall` blocks with `toolResult` messages (capped at 600 s per call), then resets the layout cache and requests a render."},"3538":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-170","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#27-lifecycle-and-ui-slots","content":"`/unipi:footer off` tears down all three slots; `/unipi:footer on` re-invokes the stored `state.setupUI` closure so the footer can be re-enabled live without a restart."},"3539":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-171","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#28-glanceeditor","content":"`glance-editor.ts` subclasses Pi's `CustomEditor`, calls `super.render()` only to obtain editor content lines, and composes a rounded frame:"},"3540":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-172","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#28-glanceeditor","content":"The status provider closure (installed from `index.ts`) supplies `workspace`, `branch`, `contextPct`, `contextWindow`, `modelName`, `thinkingLevel`, and the active `fusion` pair read via `getSharedFusionStatus()` from core. `renderFusionStatus` renders `Fusion · <lead> <effort> ◆ <sidekick>` with the lead lit and the sidekick muted, appending call split and `saved $x.xx` when available. `glanceFrameWidth(terminalWidth)` returns `max(8, terminalWidth − 1)` for the same issue-#31 reason. All keybindings, autocomplete, history and paste behaviour are inherited from the base editor; only painting changes."},"3541":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-173","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#29-tps-tracker","content":"`tps-tracker.ts` maintains one `MessageTpsRecord` per branch-local assistant message index. Two token sources are used, best-first:"},"3542":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-174","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#29-tps-tracker","content":"**Anchored** — the provider's exact `usage.output` at stream end (`message_end`); replaces any estimate."},"3543":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-175","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#29-tps-tracker","content":"**Density estimate** — `ceil(chars / 4)` accumulated over streamed `text_delta`, `thinking_delta` and `toolcall_delta` payloads while `usage.output` is still zero."},"3544":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-176","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#29-tps-tracker","content":"The timing contract is deliberately narrow: the decode window starts at the **first streamed delta** (excluding TTFT and request overhead) and ends at stream end. Tool execution and idle time are excluded, and records without a hook-measured `decodeMs` are dropped from the session average. `turn_start`/`agent_settled` and `tool_execution_start/end` hooks feed turn count, wall time and tool time for the glance session strip."},"3545":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-177","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#210-styling-layers","content":"**`theme.ts`** — capability-aware colour emission. `detectColorMode()` honours `NO_COLOR`/`NODE_DISABLE_COLORS`, `FORCE_COLOR` levels, forces Apple Terminal to 256 colours (it silently drops 24-bit escapes), recognises a list of truecolor terminals, and otherwise sniffs `TERM`. Hex colours are quantised to the nearest xterm-256 index when needed. A manual override via settings (`colorMode: truecolor | 256 | none`) wins over detection."},"3546":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-178","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#210-styling-layers","content":"**`separators.ts`** — six separator styles (`powerline`, `powerline-thin`, `slash`, `pipe`, `dot`, `ascii`) with Nerd Font glyphs or ASCII fallbacks chosen by `detectNerdFontSupport()` (`POWERLINE_NERD_FONTS` override, `GHOSTTY_RESOURCES_DIR`, known `TERM_PROGRAM` values)."},"3547":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-179","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#210-styling-layers","content":"**`icons.ts`** — `nerd` / `emoji` / `text` glyph tables selected by `setIconStyle`."},"3548":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-180","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#210-styling-layers","content":"**`lolcat.ts`** — surrogate-aware rainbow gradient used for the brand glyph."},"3549":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-181","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#210-styling-layers","content":"**`presets.ts`** — `default` (glance-style with `uni` brand, model, thinking level, directory, git on the left; context, tokens, TPS, cost, clock, duration on the right), `classic`, `minimal`, `compact`, `full`, `ascii`. Unknown names fall back to `default`."},"3550":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-182","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#211-configuration","content":"Settings live in `~/.pi/agent/settings.json` (or `$PI_AGENT_DIR/settings.json`) under `[UNIPI_SETTINGS_KEY].footer`. Defaults: `enabled: true`, `preset: \"default\"`, `glanceMode: true`, `separator: \"powerline-thin\"`, `iconStyle: \"nerd\"`, `zoneSeparator: \"│\"`, `showFullLabels: false`, `colorMode: \"auto\"`, and all groups shown except `notify`. Loading is defensive — every field is type-checked and falls back individually."},"3551":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-183","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#212-commands","content":"Command"},"3552":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-184","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#212-commands","content":"Behaviour"},"3553":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-185","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#212-commands","content":"`/unipi:footer [on\\|off]`"},"3554":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-186","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#212-commands","content":"Toggle (or explicitly set) the footer; persists `enabled`; re-installs or removes all three UI slots"},"3555":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-187","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#212-commands","content":"`/unipi:footer-settings`"},"3556":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-188","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#212-commands","content":"Three-category `SettingsList` overlay (Appearance / Segments drill-down / Labels & Help). Preset and glance flag apply live; the editor component swap is deferred until the overlay closes (`applyGlanceMode`)"},"3557":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-189","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#212-commands","content":"`/unipi:footer-help`"},"3558":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-190","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#212-commands","content":"Zone-ordered overlay listing enabled segments with icons, labels and descriptions"},"3559":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-191","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#212-commands","content":"The module announces itself with `MODULE_READY { name: \"@pi-unipi/footer\", commands: [...], tools: [] }` on `session_start`."},"3560":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-192","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#31-responsibilities","content":"Provides the `ask_user` tool so the agent can pause for a structured human decision — single-select, multi-select or freeform — and, optionally, let the user hand the conversation off to a queued follow-up command (with or without compaction first)."},"3561":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-193","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#32-tool-contract","content":"`tools.ts#registerAskUserTools` registers `ASK_USER_TOOLS.ASK` with a TypeBox schema:"},"3562":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-194","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#32-tool-contract","content":"The result carries an `AskUserResponse` in `details.response` with `kind ∈ { selection, freeform, combined, cancelled, timed_out, end_turn, new_session }` plus optional `selections`, `text`, `prefill`, `comment`, and — for handoffs — `launchedWith`, `launchStatus`, `launchReason`, `launchError`."},"3563":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-195","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#33-execution-pipeline","content":"Two guard mechanisms wrap the interactive parts:"},"3564":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-196","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#33-execution-pipeline","content":"**Settings allow-list** (`config.ts`) — `unipi.askUser` in `~/.pi/agent/settings.json` with `enabled`, `allowedFormats.{singleSelect,multiSelect,freeform}` and `notifyOnAsk` (all default `true`). Settings are cached in memory after first read."},"3565":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-197","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#33-execution-pipeline","content":"**`withHerdrBlocked`** (from core) — marks the interval during which the prompt is open so that the `herdr:blocked` signal is visible to other extensions."},"3566":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-198","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#34-tui-renderers","content":"`ask-ui.ts#renderAskUI` follows Pi's `ctx.ui.custom()` callback pattern and returns `{ render, invalidate, handleInput }`. Behaviour:"},"3567":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-199","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#34-tui-renderers","content":"Appends a synthetic &#x2A;*\"Custom response\"** option (`value: \"__freeform__\"`) when `allowFreeform` is true."},"3568":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-200","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#34-tui-renderers","content":"Single-select: arrows + Enter. Multi-select: Space toggles, Enter submits. Escape cancels. `timeout` auto-dismisses with `kind: \"timed_out\"`."},"3569":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-201","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#34-tui-renderers","content":"Freeform and `allowCustom` options open an embedded pi-tui `Editor`; per-option custom text is stored in a `Map` so multi-select can attach comments to individual choices (`kind: \"combined\"`)."},"3570":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-202","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#34-tui-renderers","content":"Line rendering goes through core's `WidthKeyedCache`, `adaptiveInnerWidth`, `contentWidth` and `shouldRenderBorder` so a resize never serves stale, over-wide lines."},"3571":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-203","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#34-tui-renderers","content":"`launcher-ui.ts#renderLauncherUI` is a three-option picker (`Compact & run 🧹`, `Run directly ▶`, `Cancel ✕`) returning `SessionLauncherResult { action, prefill }`."},"3572":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-204","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#35-handoff-semantics","content":"`handoff.ts` queues the prefill *without* waiting for an LLM turn:"},"3573":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-205","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#35-handoff-semantics","content":"**`queueDirectHandoff`** — trims the prefill (`normalizePrefill`; empty → `cancelled / empty-prefill`) and calls `pi.sendUserMessage(prefill, { deliverAs: \"followUp\" })` → `queued / direct`. If sending throws, `fallbackToEditor` places the text in the editor (`editor_prefill`) and warns the user; if even that fails, status is `failed`."},"3574":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-206","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#35-handoff-semantics","content":"**`queueCompactHandoff`** — starts `ctx.compact({ customInstructions, onComplete, onError })` and delivers exactly once via `deliverOnce&#x60;. A &#x2A;*`COMPACT_HANDOFF_FALLBACK_MS = 1500`** timer guarantees delivery (`fallback-timeout`) even if compaction callbacks wait on the tool turn. The custom instructions are prefixed with core's `COMPACTOR_INSTRUCTION` sentinel so `@pi-unipi/compactor`'s zero-LLM pipeline intercepts if installed; otherwise Pi's built-in compaction runs."},"3575":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-207","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#35-handoff-semantics","content":"Reason codes (`SessionLaunchReason`): `direct`, `compact-started`, `compacted`, `compaction-error`, `fallback-timeout`, `compact-start-failed`, `empty-prefill`, `send-failed`. Every path except `failed` ends with `ctx.abort()` so the queued command runs immediately."},"3576":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-208","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#36-commands-and-announcement","content":"`/unipi:ask-user-settings` opens `settings-tui.ts` (toggle the tool and each allowed format). On `session_start` the package emits `MODULE_READY { name: MODULES.ASK_USER, commands: [\"unipi:ask-user-settings\"], tools: [ASK_USER_TOOLS.ASK] }`."},"3577":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-209","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#41-responsibilities","content":"Adds editor-level productivity shortcuts: an ALT+S chord menu (stash/restore, undo, redo, append from register, copy, cut, toggle thinking), ALT+I tab insertion, and a `/unipi:stash-settings` overlay for keybinding customisation."},"3578":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-210","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"The header of `index.ts` states the design constraint that shapes this package:"},"3579":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-211","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"> The overlay ONLY captures action selection (pure UI, no side effects). All actions execute OUTSIDE the overlay via callbacks after `done()`."},"3580":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-212","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"`ChordOverlay` (`chord-overlay.ts`) is a `Container` implementing `Focusable` with two states — `chord_root` (action menu) and `chord_reg` (register list 0–9 + `S`) — and receives a `ChordCallbacks` bundle. When the user picks an action, the overlay calls `done()` and then the callback; the callback runs in the command context where `ctx.ui.getEditorText()` / `setEditorText()` actually work."},"3581":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-213","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"Key"},"3582":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-214","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"Action"},"3583":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-215","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"Implementation"},"3584":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-216","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"`S`"},"3585":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-217","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"Stash / Restore"},"3586":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-218","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"Non-empty editor → snapshot, save to stash, clear. Empty editor → restore stash."},"3587":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-219","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"`U` / `R`"},"3588":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-220","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"Undo / Redo"},"3589":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-221","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"`UndoRedoBuffer.undo/redo` with `suppressInputListener` set to avoid self-referencing snapshots"},"3590":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-222","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"`A` → `0–9`/`S`"},"3591":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-223","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"Append from register / stash"},"3592":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-224","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"Snapshot current text, append register contents"},"3593":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-225","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"`Y` / `D`"},"3594":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-226","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"Copy / Cut"},"3595":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-227","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#42-architectural-rule-overlays-select-callers-execute","content":"`copyToClipboard` (platform-specific); cut clears after successful copy"},"3596":{"id":"/docs/deep-explorat