/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-279","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#53-event-subscription-model","content":"`permission_request`"},"3648":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-280","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#53-event-subscription-model","content":"third-party `permissions:ui_prompt`"},"3649":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-281","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#53-event-subscription-model","content":"Permission Request"},"3650":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-282","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#53-event-subscription-model","content":"`pi.events.on`"},"3651":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-283","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#53-event-subscription-model","content":"The distinction between `pi.on` and `pi.events.on` matters operationally: lifecycle hooks are stored in the extension's handler table and replaced on reload, whereas `EventBus` listeners persist — so `registerEventListeners` first calls `unregisterAll()` on the accumulated `pi.events.on` unsubscribers to avoid duplicate notifications after a reload. Per-event enablement and platform lists come from `config.events[eventKey]`."},"3652":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-284","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#53-event-subscription-model","content":"Agent lifecycle events use a dedicated `registerAgentNotification` path that adds two behaviours: **wake-task suppression** and **recap**."},"3653":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-285","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#54-wake-task-suppression-via-shared-registry","content":"`hasPendingWakeTask()` reads `globalThis[Symbol.for(\"unipi.background-tasks.shared-registry\")]` and returns true if any task is `running` with `triggerOnCompletion === true`. The rationale in the source: such a task will wake the agent in a fresh turn that produces its own `agent_end`, so notifying for the intermediate turn would duplicate the message. The symbol is read directly \"so notify has zero load-order or dependency coupling to that optional sibling\"; any read failure means \"no pending wake\"."},"3654":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-286","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#55-dispatch-pipeline","content":"**Priority mapping** — `mapNotifyPriority`: Gotify `low 2 / normal 5 / high 8`; ntfy `low 2 / normal 3 / high 5`. Native and Telegram ignore numeric priority."},"3655":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-287","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#55-dispatch-pipeline","content":"**Suppression is not failure.** `native.ts` throws `SuppressedError` when `suppressWhenFocused` is on and `isWindowFocused()` (currently implemented on Windows) is true; dispatch records it as `success: true, suppressed: true`."},"3656":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-288","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#55-dispatch-pipeline","content":"**Silence after input** (`activity.ts`) — `noteInput()` is called from `ctx.ui.onTerminalInput`; when `silenceAfterInput.enabled` and the last keypress is within `windowMs`, listed platforms (or all, if the list is empty) are silenced. `ask_user_prompt` and `permission_request` are **blocking events** and always bypass this filter because the keypress that caused them must not mute them."},"3657":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-289","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#55-dispatch-pipeline","content":"**Renotify** — `RenotifyConfig { enabled, intervalMs, maxRepeats }` re-sends unanswered human-blocking prompts; any keypress calls `disarmRenotify()`."},"3658":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-290","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#55-dispatch-pipeline","content":"Message builders: `buildAskUserPromptMessage` accepts both Unipi's flat payload and the rpiv questionnaire projection (`Agent asks: <question> (+n more) — opt1, opt2`); `buildPermissionPromptMessage` handles the permission-system payload."},"3659":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-291","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#56-recap-summarisation","content":"When `config.recap.enabled`, agent-end notifications summarise the last assistant message before sending. The text is taken from the payload or, for `agent_settled` (which carries no messages), from `sessionCtx.sessionManager.getEntries()`. The configured model (`provider/modelId`) is resolved through `sessionCtx.modelRegistry`, credentials fetched with `getApiKeyAndHeaders`, and `summarizeLastMessage` routes to `anthropic-messages` or an OpenAI-compatible endpoint with `MAX_INPUT_CHARS = 2000`, `MAX_TOKENS = 100`, `TIMEOUT_MS = 10 000`. `disableThinking` sends `chat_template_kwargs` to stop llama.cpp/vLLM-style thinking models from spending the budget on reasoning (issue #36). Any failure falls back to a 100-character truncation, then to the plain lifecycle message."},"3660":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-292","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"Platform"},"3661":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-293","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"File"},"3662":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-294","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"Transport"},"3663":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-295","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"Required config"},"3664":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-296","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"Native"},"3665":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-297","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"`platforms/native.ts`"},"3666":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-298","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"`node-notifier` (SnoreToast / terminal-notifier / notify-send)"},"3667":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-299","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"`native.enabled`, optional `windowsAppId`, `suppressWhenFocused`"},"3668":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-300","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"ntfy"},"3669":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-301","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"`platforms/ntfy.ts`"},"3670":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-302","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"HTTP publish to topic"},"3671":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-303","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"project/global `ntfy.json`: `serverUrl`, `topic`, optional `token`, `priority`"},"3672":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-304","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"Gotify"},"3673":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-305","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"`platforms/gotify.ts`"},"3674":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-306","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"HTTP message API"},"3675":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-307","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"`serverUrl`, `appToken`, `priority`"},"3676":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-308","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"Telegram"},"3677":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-309","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"`platforms/telegram.ts`"},"3678":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-310","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"Bot API"},"3679":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-311","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"`botToken`, `chatId`"},"3680":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-312","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#57-platform-adapters","content":"`NotifyPlatform` is the union `\"native\" | \"gotify\" | \"telegram\" | \"ntfy\"`; `focus.ts`/`focus-win.ts` are helpers for foreground-window detection rather than a delivery platform."},"3681":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-313","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#58-tool-commands-lifecycle","content":"**`notify_user`** tool (`tools.ts`): `{ message, title?, priority?, platforms? }`; dispatches fire-and-forget with `eventType: \"agent_tool\"` and returns per-platform numeric priorities in `details`."},"3682":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-314","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#58-tool-commands-lifecycle","content":"**Commands**: `unipi:notify-settings`, `unipi:notify-set-gotify`, `unipi:notify-set-tg`, `unipi:notify-set-ntfy`, `unipi:notify-test`, `unipi:notify-recap-model` — each backed by a setup overlay under `tui/`."},"3683":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-315","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#58-tool-commands-lifecycle","content":"**Lifecycle**: on `session_start` the package stores the session context, resets input activity, subscribes to terminal input, loads config, registers listeners, and emits `MODULE_READY`. On `session_shutdown` it unsubscribes terminal input, disarms renotify, clears context and unregisters `EventBus` listeners."},"3684":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-316","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#61-info-screen-pi-unipiinfo-screen","content":"**InfoRegistry** (`registry.ts`) is a cache-first reactive store exposed as `globalThis.__unipi_info_registry` so other packages can `registerGroup` without importing the package:"},"3685":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-317","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#61-info-screen-pi-unipiinfo-screen","content":"`registerGroup(group)` stores `{ id, name, icon, priority, config.stats[], dataProvider }` and fires a synthetic update so open overlays re-sync their group list."},"3686":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-318","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#61-info-screen-pi-unipiinfo-screen","content":"`getGroupData(id)` returns cached data if younger than `cacheTtlMs = 5000`, otherwise awaits `dataProvider()`, deduplicating concurrent fetches through an `inflight` map. Provider errors return the last cached value."},"3687":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-319","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#61-info-screen-pi-unipiinfo-screen","content":"`refreshGroup`/`refreshAll` are fire-and-forget; `subscribeAll(cb)` delivers `(groupId, data)`; `getVisibleStats` filters by user config; `invalidateCache` drops a group."},"3688":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-320","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#61-info-screen-pi-unipiinfo-screen","content":"**Extension entry** (`index.ts`):"},"3689":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-321","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#61-info-screen-pi-unipiinfo-screen","content":"Registers core groups synchronously and starts load-time tracking."},"3690":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-322","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#61-info-screen-pi-unipiinfo-screen","content":"Batches `MODULE_READY` announcements with a 150 ms debounce, records module versions, load times and tools (`trackModule`, `trackTool`), invalidates `overview`/`tools`, and only re-fetches when an overlay is actually visible."},"3691":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-323","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#61-info-screen-pi-unipiinfo-screen","content":"Tracks built-in tool usage via `pi.on(\"tool_call\")`."},"3692":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-324","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#61-info-screen-pi-unipiinfo-screen","content":"**Boot splash**: if `settings.bootMode !== \"off\"` and `event.reason === \"startup\"`, the overlay opens immediately. In `auto-close` mode it is **non-capturing** (never takes keyboard focus), dismisses itself via `handle.hide()` after `bootTimeoutMs`, and only does so while it is the top-most *visible* overlay — dismissing a covered entry would orphan whatever overlay is on top (e.g. a hung `ctx.ui.select` in the updater prompt)."},"3693":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-325","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#61-info-screen-pi-unipiinfo-screen","content":"Commands: `/unipi:info` (interactive overlay, 80 % width, centered) and `/unipi:info-settings`."},"3694":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-326","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#62-command-enchantment-packagesautocomplete--pi-unipicommand-enchantment","content":"On `session_start`, if `isAutocompleteEnhanced()` (persisted in `~/.unipi/config/command-enchantment/config.json`, default `true`), the package wraps Pi's base autocomplete provider via `ctx.ui.addAutocompleteProvider((current) => createEnchantedProvider(current, true))`. When disabled it registers nothing."},"3695":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-327","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#62-command-enchantment-packagesautocomplete--pi-unipicommand-enchantment","content":"`createEnchantedProvider` intercepts only slash-command positions:"},"3696":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-328","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#62-command-enchantment-packagesautocomplete--pi-unipicommand-enchantment","content":"**Argument position** (`isInUnipiArgPosition`) — delegates to the base provider with `force: false` so Tab after a `/unipi:*` command returns argument completions rather than file suggestions; `shouldTriggerFileCompletion` returns `true` in that context to keep the call path open."},"3697":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-329","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#62-command-enchantment-packagesautocomplete--pi-unipicommand-enchantment","content":"**Command-name position** — fetches base suggestions, strips Pi's source tags (`[u:npm:@pi-unipi/unipi]`) from `unipi:*` descriptions (`stripPiSourceTag`), then regenerates `unipi:*` items from `COMMAND_REGISTRY` with package-coloured tags (`[workflow]`, `[memory]`, …)."},"3698":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-330","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#62-command-enchantment-packagesautocomplete--pi-unipicommand-enchantment","content":"**Namespace boost** (`detectNamespaceBoost`) — queries equal to a package name or alias (`mem`, `ms`, `goal`, `util`, `web`, `notification`, …) return *all* of that package's commands first."},"3699":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-331","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#62-command-enchantment-packagesautocomplete--pi-unipicommand-enchantment","content":"**Cross-group ranking** (`sorting.ts#sortTaggedItems`) — four tiers: exact full-value match, `unipi:` short-name exact match, prefix match, fuzzy match; within a tier non-unipi (system) commands sort first, and fuzzy ties prefer shorter names. `skill:` items are hidden unless the user explicitly typed `/skill:`."},"3700":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-332","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#63-btw-pi-unipibtw","content":"`extensions/btw.ts` (\\~2 k lines, adapted from pi-btw) opens a genuine Pi sub-session using `createAgentSession` with read-only coding-tool access so the user can ask side questions while the main agent is busy. Key elements:"},"3701":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-333","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#63-btw-pi-unipibtw","content":"**Commands**: `/unipi:btw [--save] <question>` (contextual), `/unipi:btw-tangent [--save] <q>` (contextless), `/unipi:btw-new [question]`, `/unipi:btw-clear`, `/unipi:btw-inject [instructions]`, `/unipi:btw-summarize [instructions]`."},"3702":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-334","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#63-btw-pi-unipibtw","content":"**System prompt** enforces the read-only aside: the model may read/search files but must never claim to have edited or executed anything, and should direct the user to `btw-inject`/`btw-summarize` for handoff."},"3703":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-335","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#63-btw-pi-unipibtw","content":"**Transcript state machine** — `BtwTranscriptEntry` variants (`turn-boundary`, `user-message`, `thinking`, `assistant-text`, `tool-call`, `tool-result`) with streaming flags drive the overlay renderer."},"3704":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-336","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#63-btw-pi-unipibtw","content":"**Persistence into the main session** uses custom message types `btw-note`, `btw-thread-entry`, `btw-thread-reset`."},"3705":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-337","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#63-btw-pi-unipibtw","content":"**Focus shortcuts** `Alt+/` and `Ctrl+Alt+W` (`matchesBtwFocusShortcut`) bring the overlay into focus."},"3706":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-338","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#71-integration-channels-used-by-this-domain","content":"Channel"},"3707":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-339","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#71-integration-channels-used-by-this-domain","content":"Used by"},"3708":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-340","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#71-integration-channels-used-by-this-domain","content":"Purpose"},"3709":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-341","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#71-integration-channels-used-by-this-domain","content":"`pi.events` (`UNIPI_EVENTS`)"},"3710":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-342","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#71-integration-channels-used-by-this-domain","content":"footer (`events.ts`), notify (`events.ts`), info-screen (`MODULE_READY`)"},"3711":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-343","page_id"