ation/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#73-configuration-persistence","content":"`.unipi/config/input-shortcuts.json`, `.unipi/config/input-shortcuts-config.json`"},"3753":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-385","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#73-configuration-persistence","content":"registers/stash · chord/tab keys"},"3754":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-386","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#73-configuration-persistence","content":"command-enchantment"},"3755":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-387","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#73-configuration-persistence","content":"`~/.unipi/config/command-enchantment/config.json`"},"3756":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-388","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#73-configuration-persistence","content":"`autocompleteEnhanced`"},"3757":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-389","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#73-configuration-persistence","content":"info-screen"},"3758":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-390","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#73-configuration-persistence","content":"package config (`config.ts`)"},"3759":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-391","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#73-configuration-persistence","content":"`bootMode`, `bootTimeoutMs`, per-stat visibility"},"3760":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-392","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#74-terminal-rendering-invariants","content":"Several files converge on the same defensive rules, which any new UI in this domain should follow:"},"3761":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-393","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#74-terminal-rendering-invariants","content":"**Never write the last column.** Frame width, process line, session strip and top widget all cap at `width − 1` (issue #31)."},"3762":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-394","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#74-terminal-rendering-invariants","content":"**Measure with `visibleWidth`, never `String.length`.** ANSI SGR, OSC 133 prompt markers and Pi's APC cursor marker are zero-width and must be skipped by both painting and width math (`glance-editor.ts#ANSI_RE`)."},"3763":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-395","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#74-terminal-rendering-invariants","content":"**Key caches by width.** `WidthKeyedCache` (core) is used by ask-user and launcher UIs so a resize cannot serve stale lines."},"3764":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-396","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#74-terminal-rendering-invariants","content":"**Overlays must be stack-aware.** Popping via `done()` removes the *top-most* overlay; self-dismissing overlays use `handle.hide()` and check they are top-most visible first (info-screen), and the footer restores focus after swapping the editor component."},"3765":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-397","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#74-terminal-rendering-invariants","content":"**Never log to stdout from render paths.** `FooterRegistry.log` is a deliberate no-op."},"3766":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-398","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#9-design-observations-and-technical-notes","content":"**Strengths**"},"3767":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-399","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#9-design-observations-and-technical-notes","content":"**Segment renderers are pure functions** of `FooterSegmentContext`, which keeps the footer extensible: adding a module means adding a `FooterGroup` and, optionally, a handler in `events.ts`."},"3768":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-400","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#9-design-observations-and-technical-notes","content":"**Fail-soft everywhere.** Event handlers, subscriber callbacks, TPS hooks, settings loaders and platform sends are all wrapped so a single bad payload cannot take down the TUI or a lifecycle hook."},"3769":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-401","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#9-design-observations-and-technical-notes","content":"**Guard-rails precede side effects.** `ask_user` validates settings, formats and UI availability before rendering; `notify` resolves and filters platforms before any network call; the chord overlay executes nothing until it has closed."},"3770":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-402","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#9-design-observations-and-technical-notes","content":"**Careful terminal hygiene** (width −1, zero-width sequence stripping, overlay-stack awareness) encoded as reusable helpers and explained in comments with issue references."},"3771":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-403","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#9-design-observations-and-technical-notes","content":"**Points to be aware of**"},"3772":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-404","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#9-design-observations-and-technical-notes","content":"**Two strategies for the same registry.** `footer/process-line.ts` imports `getSharedTaskRegistry` from `@pi-unipi/background-tasks` (a hard `package.json` dependency), whereas `notify/events.ts` reads the `Symbol.for` slot directly to avoid coupling. Both work, but only one of them keeps the \"core-only internal dependency\" rule."},"3773":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-405","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#9-design-observations-and-technical-notes","content":"**Multiple global registries.** The footer registry is a module singleton, the info registry is a string-keyed `globalThis` property, and fusion/background-tasks use `Symbol.for`. New consumers should prefer typed accessors in core (as `getSharedFusionStatus` does)."},"3774":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-406","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#9-design-observations-and-technical-notes","content":"**MCP tool-count bookkeeping is approximate.** `MCP_SERVER_STOPPED` subtracts tools only when the stopped server matches `lastServerStarted`; the `globalThis.__unipi_mcp_stats` escape hatch exists precisely to allow the MCP package to publish authoritative counts."},"3775":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-407","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#9-design-observations-and-technical-notes","content":"**`notify/events.ts` header vs. implementation.** The file header advertises \"dynamic discovery via MODULE\\_READY\", but the subscription set observed in `registerEventListeners` is the static `BUILTIN_EVENTS` table (plus two third-party event strings). Operators should treat the table as the source of truth for which events can notify."},"3776":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-408","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#9-design-observations-and-technical-notes","content":"**`MODULE_READY` timing differs.** Most packages emit it on `session_start`; `input-shortcuts` emits at load time. Consumers that subscribe on `session_start` may therefore miss the latter's announcement."},"3777":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-409","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#9-design-observations-and-technical-notes","content":"**`footer/src/index.ts` (\\~660 lines)** concentrates lifecycle, TPS reconciliation, glance installation and strip rendering; the reconciliation scan in particular re-walks the whole branch every second."},"3778":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-410","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#9-design-observations-and-technical-notes","content":"**Preset name drift.** Earlier research listed a `nerd` preset; the code defines `default`, `classic`, `minimal`, `compact`, `full`, `ascii`. Nerd-Font behaviour is controlled by `iconStyle` and separator detection rather than a preset."},"3779":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-411","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#101-commands","content":"Command"},"3780":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-412","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#101-commands","content":"Package"},"3781":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-413","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#101-commands","content":"`/unipi:footer [on\\|off]`, `/unipi:footer-settings`, `/unipi:footer-help`"},"3782":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-414","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#101-commands","content":"footer"},"3783":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-415","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#101-commands","content":"`/unipi:ask-user-settings`"},"3784":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-416","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#101-commands","content":"ask-user"},"3785":{"id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain-417","page_id":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deep-exploration/user-interaction-and-presentation-domain#101-commands","content":"`/u