l` / `⚡ wf ○ rl`. It also subscribes to `MODULE_READY` and flips `ralphDetected` when `MODULES.RALPH` announces itself, so load order is irrelevant. `session_shutdown` resets all three pieces of state."],[531,"**`@pi-unipi/core` (\\~58 KB, zero internal dependencies).** `index.ts` re-exports `constants`, `events`, `sandbox`, `utils`, `model-cache`, `tui-overlay`, `tui-width`, `spinner-line`, `bounded-output`, and `fusion-status`. The two `Symbol.for` slots (`unipi.background-tasks.shared-registry`, `unipi.fusion.status`) are typed accessors that return `undefined` when the producer is absent, allowing consumers to degrade gracefully."],[2264,"**`autoCompaction`** (see §2.6)."],[533,"**`background-tasks/registry.ts` (`BackgroundTaskRegistry`).** Spawns child processes with `UNIPI_BG_*` env, tails stdout, recognises XML usage blocks and normalises them into a uniform usage record (model, context, tokens, tools), persists periodic snapshots, and exposes `allTasks()` synchronously through the shared symbol for the footer's 1-second refresh."],[3128,"**`CheckboxParser` (`parser/checkbox-parser.ts`).** A config-driven class that, per its header comment, replaces seven previously separate parser classes. Each `CheckboxDocConfig` supplies:"],[2204,"**`compile(input)`** — the unranked path. The brief transcript is built from all filtered blocks and capped at `BRIEF_MAX_LINES = 120`."],[2205,"**`compileRanked(input)`** — the path used by the live compaction hook. Blocks are first scored and selected under a character budget (`selectRankedBriefBlocks`), the fresh brief is **not** capped, and merging preserves the fresh brief (`preserveFreshBriefOnMerge: true`)."],[2472,"**`connect(command, args, env)`** spawns the process with `stdio: [\"pipe\",\"pipe\",\"pipe\"]` and `{...process.env, ...env}`, then sends `initialize` with `protocolVersion: \"2024-11-05\"` and `clientInfo: { name: \"@pi-unipi/mcp\" }`. On success it sends the `notifications/initialized` notification and marks